\HLASourcePage{49}{48}
\HLAAnchor{clause:4.1.4.1}
\pdfbookmark[3]{4.1.4.1 Rules for combining information from FOM modules}{bookmark:clause:4.1.4.1}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the \emph{Create Federation Execution} service is invoked, the RTI shall initialize the federation execution\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 using FDD first from the MIM and then from the specified FOM modules. A user-extended MIM may be\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{309.912}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 provided; otherwise, the RTI shall provide the standard MIM automatically.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Additional FOM modules may be provided in the \emph{Join Federation Execution} service invocations. The FOM\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 module designator arguments supplied to the \emph{Create Federation Execution} service and the \emph{Join Federation}\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Execution} service shall designate compliant FOM modules (IEEE Std 1516-2025 and IEEE Std 1516.2-\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2025). \emph{Create Federation Execution} and \emph{Join Federation Execution} service invocations shall reject, issuing\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{165.784}{251.939}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 an exception, any entity that is not a compliant FOM module.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{189.644}{287.557}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{4.1.4.1 Rules for combining information from FOM modules}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{213.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall combine the FDD data of the MIM and FOM modules according to the rules for combining\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{225.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 FOM data in IEEE Std 1516.2-2025 when the \emph{Create Federation Execution} service is invoked as well as\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{237.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 whenever the set of FOM modules has changed due to an invocation of the \emph{Join Federation Execution}\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{249.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service. The RTI shall consider only the FDD when combining FOM modules. After combining switches\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{261.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 from all FDD provided during the Create Federation Execution service, if a switch remains unspecified, the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{273.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 RTI shall provide a default value for the switch in the current FOM as specified in IEEE Std 1516.2-2025. In\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{285.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 case the FDD of the FOM modules provided in such a service call cannot be successfully combined or the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{297.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation fails for any other reason, the FDD provided in the call shall not be included in the current FOM.\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{321.782}{415.062}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall reject, issuing an exception, any attempt to load a FOM module for the following cases:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{345.781}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{345.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named object class attribute that has different transportation or order when\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{357.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 compared to an already existing named object class attribute with the same name and belonging to\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{369.781}{172.529}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the same object class in the current FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{384.781}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{384.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named interaction class that has different transportation or order when\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{396.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 compared to an already existing named interaction class with the same qualified name in the current\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{408.780}{30.145}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{423.780}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{423.780}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named dimension that has different upper bound or value when unspecified\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{435.780}{313.576}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 when compared to an already existing named dimension in the current FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{450.780}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{450.780}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named transportation type that has a different reliability when compared to\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{462.780}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 an already existing named transportation type in the current FOM. (Comment note - description is\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{474.779}{290.450}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 not part of FDD nor should it be and thus cannot be used for rejection.)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{489.779}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{489.779}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named update rate that has a different maximum rate when compared to an\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{501.779}{227.783}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 already existing named update rate in the current FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{516.779}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{516.779}{400.018}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When trying to define a named switch that has a different definition when compared to an already\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{528.778}{177.910}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 existing named switch in the current FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{543.778}{15.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{543.778}{204.835}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the MIM or FOM module is noncompliant.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{567.778}{431.997}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If a FOM module or MIM contains any definition that is rejected by the RTI, the RTI shall reject the FOM\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{579.778}{297.214}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 module or MIM in its entirety and shall not add any element to the FDD.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{603.777}{431.997}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The union of all FOM modules in a given \emph{Create Federation Execution} or \emph{Join Federation Execution}\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{615.777}{431.997}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service when added to the previously existing current FOM shall not result in any object class or interaction\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{627.777}{431.997}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class not having a full definition. If this is the case, the entire service invocation shall fail. In case any of the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{639.777}{376.295}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 FOM modules provided was rejected by the RTI, the entire service invocation shall also fail.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{663.776}{431.998}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 After a \emph{Create Federation Execution} or \emph{Join Federation Execution} service has completed successfully, all\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{675.776}{431.999}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the provided FOM modules shall be available in the current FOM, and the corresponding MOM information\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{687.776}{128.639}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be updated to reflect this.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{50}{49}
\HLAAnchor{clause:4.1.4.2}
\pdfbookmark[3]{4.1.4.2 Access to Current FOM information}{bookmark:clause:4.1.4.2}
\HLAAnchor{clause:4.1.5}
\pdfbookmark[2]{4.1.5 Logical time implementation}{bookmark:clause:4.1.5}
\HLAAnchor{clause:4.1.6}
\pdfbookmark[2]{4.1.6 Fault tolerance support}{bookmark:clause:4.1.6}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Furthermore, any FDD provided as per above, once available in the federation execution, shall be available\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{224.492}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 for the remaining life span of the federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.646}{210.888}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{4.1.4.2 Access to Current FOM information }%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall provide access to the current FDD, the content of individual FOM modules, as well as the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{221.131}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 MIM. The following MOM interactions are provided:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{165.784}{13.761}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{165.784}{121.805}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For the federation execution:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{180.784}{14.298}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{180.784}{379.980}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The attribute HLAFOMmoduleDesignatorList provides a list of designators for the FOM\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{192.784}{379.980}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 modules that specified the current FOM. Only FOM modules that resulted in the addition or\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{204.784}{379.980}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 modification of one or more classes, directed interactions, dimensions, transportations, update\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{216.783}{379.980}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 rates, or switches shall be included. Specifically, if several FOM modules with identical\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{228.783}{379.980}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 content have been specified, only the first shall be included and then only if it satisfies the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{240.783}{98.648}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 preceding requirement.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{255.783}{14.313}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.036}{255.783}{379.964}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The attribute HLAfederation.HLAMIMDesignator provides the designator for the MIM used in\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{267.783}{75.633}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the current FOM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{282.782}{14.305}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 3)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.029}{282.782}{297.403}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The attribute HLAcurrentFDD provides the contents of the current FDD.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{297.782}{14.299}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 4)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.023}{297.782}{379.977}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The interactions HLArequestFOMmoduleData and HLAreportFOMmoduleData provide the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{309.782}{154.764}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 contents of a specified FOM module.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{324.782}{14.313}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 5)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.037}{324.782}{379.963}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The interactions HLArequestMIMData and HLAreportMIMData provides the content of the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{336.781}{29.557}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 MIM.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{351.781}{14.320}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.945}{351.781}{78.245}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For each federate:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{366.781}{14.314}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.038}{366.781}{379.962}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The attribute HLAfederate.HLAFOMmoduleDesignatorList provides a list of designators for\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{378.781}{379.979}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the FOM modules that were specified by that federate when invoking the \emph{Create Federation}\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{390.781}{205.302}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Execution} and \emph{Join Federation Execution} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{405.780}{14.299}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{405.780}{379.978}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The interactions HLArequestFOMmoduleData and HLAreportFOMmoduleData provide the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{417.780}{154.764}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 contents of a specified FOM module.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{441.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A FOM module designator shall be equal to the string (file name or URL) as supplied as part of the \emph{Create}\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{453.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Federation Execution }or \emph{Join Federation Execution} service invocation. The FOM module designator for the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{465.779}{354.072}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 HLAstandardMIM as supplied automatically by the RTI shall be “HLAstandardMIM.”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{489.640}{165.957}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{4.1.5 Logical time implementation}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{513.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI and joined federates of a federation execution shall share a common implementation of logical time\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{525.778}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in order to have meaningful interactions involving logical time. No universal implementation of logical time\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{537.778}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 has been proposed that will satisfy all federation executions. When a federation execution is created, a\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{549.778}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 logical time implementation shall be identified. RTIs shall provide two default implementations of logical\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{561.778}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 time, one integer and one floating point. The federate creating a federation execution may provide its own\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{573.778}{271.313}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 implementation of logical time for use in the federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{597.638}{142.055}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{4.1.6 Fault tolerance support}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{621.777}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A fault shall have occurred if at any point during a federation execution an unexpected event prevents one or\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{633.777}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 more joined federates in the federation from executing in an HLA-compliant manner. The criteria and\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{645.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 detection methods of a fault depend on the technical implementation of the RTI and are not part of the HLA\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{657.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 standard. A fault may result in one or more federates being disconnected or lost from the federation. Such a\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{669.776}{190.274}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate shall be referred to as a lost federate. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{693.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A fault may divide the federation into multiple independent segments, each having the potential to continue\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{705.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 as an HLA-compliant federation execution. In this situation, the RTI shall select exactly one such segment to\linebreak%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{51}{50}
\HLAAnchor{clause:4.1.7}
\pdfbookmark[2]{4.1.7 Authorization}{bookmark:clause:4.1.7}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 continue the federation execution. Federates contained in all other segments shall be considered lost. It may\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be that the fault is catastrophic with no segment remaining to continue the federation execution. The\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{299.966}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 mechanism for making these decisions is RTI implementation dependent.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a fault occurs and there are still joined federates in the federation, those joined federates which are\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscribed to the HLAreportFederateLost MOM interaction shall receive the interaction for each lost\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate. If a lost federate was time regulating, this interaction shall provide its last known time position.\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The last known time position shall be determined by the RTI for a lost federate so that all TSO messages\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 sent by the lost federate with timestamps less than or equal to the last known time position shall be delivered\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 to the subscribed joined federates that remain in the federation. TSO messages with timestamps greater than\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{189.784}{418.948}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 this point and RO messages from the lost federate may or may not be delivered to subscribed federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{213.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 After reporting lost federates using the HLAreportFederateLost MOM interaction, the RTI shall then\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{225.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 perform a resign on behalf of each lost federate, using each federate\textquotesingle{}s Automatic Resign Directive. All\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{237.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federation-wide synchronized operations with the remaining joined federates shall continue as if the lost\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{249.783}{367.431}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates had resigned. MOM data and advisories shall be updated to reflect the new state.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{273.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a federate becomes lost, the RTI may attempt to notify it using the \emph{Connection Lost \textdagger{}} service\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{285.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation. A successful invocation of the \emph{Connection Lost \textdagger{}} service by the RTI on the federate shall enter\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{297.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the federate into the Not Connected state (see Figure 3). Because a lost federate or its environment is subject\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{309.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 to a fault, a federate that has been reported to the federation execution as lost but has not received the\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{321.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Connection Lost \textdagger{}} service invocation is in an undefined state. A lost federate may try to connect to the RTI\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{333.782}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and join the federation execution again using the connect and join sequence. The attempts may or may not\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{345.781}{329.106}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be successful, depending on the fault and steps taken outside of HLA to repair it.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{369.642}{95.373}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{4.1.7 Authorization}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{393.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Authorization makes it possible to control if a federate is allowed to connect to an RTI, and which\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{405.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federations that it is allowed to create, join and destroy. An RTI shall be configurable to require\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{417.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 authorization or not, and if so, what authorization service to use. If authorization is required, federates shall\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{429.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 provide credentials as part of the Connect service invocation. If an RTI has been configured for\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{441.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 authorization, the RTI shall verify if a service invocation is permitted, given the credentials of a federate, by\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{453.780}{136.469}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 calling the authorization service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{477.779}{432.003}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Credentials may be of different types, for example passwords or certificates, depending on the configured\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{489.779}{94.231}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 type of authorization. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{513.779}{350.808}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following HLA services may or may not be permitted, based on these credentials:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.017}{533.819}{13.758}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{533.819}{39.310}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Connect%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.017}{545.819}{14.356}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{545.819}{277.121}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Create Federation Execution, for a given federation execution name%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.017}{557.819}{13.746}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.966}{557.819}{400.034}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Join Federation Execution, for a given federation execution name, federate name and federate type%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.017}{569.819}{14.356}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{569.819}{282.768}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Destroy Federation Execution, for a given federation execution name%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{593.818}{385.185}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In case a service invocation is not permitted, it shall fail, and the RTI shall throw an exception.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{617.818}{432.003}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The authorization service is specified in 12.5. It shall only be possible to configure one authorization service\linebreak%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{629.818}{72.867}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 for a given RTI. %
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

