 \HLAServiceHeadingAt{375.383}{%
 4.19\ \emph{Request Federation Save}\ service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{400.806}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The\ \emph{Request Federation Save}\ service shall specify that a federation save should take place.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{424.805}{432.000}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the optional timestamp argument is not present, the RTI shall instruct all federation execution members to\linebreak%
 save state as soon as possible after the invocation of the\ \emph{Request Federation Save}\ service.\ %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{460.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An optional timestamp argument may be supplied only if the joined federate is time-regulating or if the\linebreak%
 Greatest Available Logical Time (GALT) is defined for the joined federate. Supplied timestamp arguments\linebreak%
 shall be larger than the time position of all time-constrained joined federates in the federation execution. For\linebreak%
 time-regulating joined federates, this is ensured by using only timestamps that are valid for the joined\linebreak%
 federate to send in a TSO message (see 8.1 for more information on valid TSO message timestamps). For\linebreak%
 nonregulating joined federates at which GALT is defined, this can be ensured by only using timestamps that\linebreak%
 are greater than the joined federate’s GALT value.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{556.803}{432.001}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If a valid optional timestamp argument is present, the RTI shall instruct each time-constrained joined\linebreak%
 federate to save state (via the\ \emph{Initiate Federate Save \textdagger{}}\ service) as soon as the joined federate has received all\linebreak%
 messages that it will receive as TSO messages that have timestamps less than or equal to the timestamp of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{590.550}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the scheduled save\HLASupMark{16}\ and either%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{607.805}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{607.805}{400.020}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate is in the Time Advancing state as a result of invocation of a\ \emph{Time Advance}\linebreak%
 \emph{Request Available},\ \emph{Next Message Request Available}, or\ \emph{Flush Queue Request}\ service and the\linebreak%
 timestamp of the next grant is greater than the timestamp of the scheduled save, or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{646.805}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{646.805}{400.021}{\rmfamily}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate is in the Time Advancing state as a result of invocation of either a\ \emph{Time Advance}\linebreak%
 \emph{Request}\ or\ \emph{Next Message Request}\ service and the timestamp of the next grant is greater than or equal\linebreak%
 to the timestamp of the scheduled save%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{707.250}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{7.98}{9.40}{%
 \HLASupMark{16}In other words, the federate’s GALT will always be greater than the timestamp of the scheduled save.%
 }
