 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Figure 13 depicts the state of an arbitrary interaction class and shows the properties relating to interaction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 classes that may be controlled by a joined federate. Specifically, a joined federate may publish or subscribe%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 to interaction classes.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may also direct the RTI via the \emph{Enable/Disable Interaction Relevance Advisory Switch}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 services to indicate that the joined federate does or does not want the RTI to use the \emph{Turn Interactions On \textdagger{}}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{141.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and \emph{Turn Interactions Off \textdagger{} }services to inform the joined federate when interactions of a given class are%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{153.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 relevant to the other joined federates in the federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{233.940}{527.026}{288.060}{\sffamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
