\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.120}{432.000}{\sffamily\bfseries\raggedright}{12.00}{14.00}{%
 6. Object management%
 }
 \HLAServiceHeadingAt{97.403}{%
 6.1 Overview%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{122.766}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 This group of HLA services shall deal with the registration, modification, and deletion of object instances%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{134.765}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and the sending and receipt of interactions.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{156.646}{%
 6.1.1 Object instance discovery%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{180.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Object instance discovery is a prime concept in this service group. Object instance \emph{O} shall have a candidate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{192.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 discovery class at joined federate \emph{F} if joined federate \emph{F} is subscribed to either the registered class of \emph{O} or to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{204.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a superclass of the registered class of \emph{O}. (A joined federate \emph{F} may be subscribed either by the DM%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{216.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscription service \emph{Subscribe Object Class Attributes} or by the DDM subscription service\emph{ Subscribe Object}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{228.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Class Attributes With Regions}.) If an object instance has a candidate discovery class at a joined federate, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{240.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 candidate discovery class of the object instance at that joined federate shall be the object instance’s%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{252.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 registered class if subscribed to by the joined federate. Otherwise, the candidate discovery class of the object%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{264.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance shall be the closest superclass of the object instances’s registered class to which the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{276.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 is subscribed.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{300.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate discovers an object instance via the \emph{Discover Object Instance \textdagger{}} service. This service shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{312.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be invoked at a joined federate \emph{F} for object instance \emph{O} when%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{327.782}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{327.782}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{O }is not known at\emph{ F, }and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{342.782}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.946}{342.782}{400.054}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There is an instance attribute \emph{i} of \emph{O }that has a corresponding class attribute \emph{i', }and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{357.782}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{357.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{i }is owned by\emph{ }either another joined federate (not \emph{F}) or the RTI, and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{372.782}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.962}{372.782}{400.038}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Either%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{387.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{387.781}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{i'} is a subscribed attribute of\emph{ O}’s candidate discovery class, or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{402.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{402.781}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{i'} is a subscribed attribute of\emph{ O}’s candidate discovery class with regions and the update region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{414.781}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 set of \emph{i} by the owning joined federate overlaps the subscription region set of \emph{i'} at \emph{O}’s candidate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{426.781}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 discovery class at the subscribing joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{448.800}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the \emph{Discover Object Instance \textdagger{}} service is invoked, the class that is an argument to this service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{460.800}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation shall be called the discovered class of the object instance. At the moment of discovery, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{472.800}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 discovered class shall be the same as the candidate discovery class. Subsequent to discovery, the discovered%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{484.800}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class cannot change. The candidate discovery class may change. As long as an object instance remains%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{496.800}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known, however, its candidate discovery class is not of interest.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{518.819}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a joined federate either uses the \emph{Register Object Instance} service to register an object instance or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{528.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 receives an invocation of the \emph{Discover Object Instance \textdagger{} }to discover an object instance, that object instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{538.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 becomes known to the joined federate, and the object instance has a known class at that joined federate. If a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{548.825}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate knows about an object instance as a result of having registered it, that object instance’s%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{558.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known class is its registered class. If the joined federate knows about the object instance as a result of having%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{568.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 discovered it, the object instance’s known class is its discovered class.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{590.685}{%
 6.1.2 Scope%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{614.824}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the \emph{Discover Object Instance \textdagger{}} service is invoked, there shall be an instance attribute that is part of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{626.824}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 newly discovered object instance that immediately comes into scope at the discovering joined federate, both%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{638.824}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 when DDM is used and when it is not used. An instance attribute of an object instance shall be in scope for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{650.823}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate \emph{F} if%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{665.823}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{665.823}{400.023}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The object instance is known to the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{680.823}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{680.823}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The instance attribute is owned by another joined federate or by the RTI, and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{695.823}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.976}{695.823}{400.024}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Either:%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{109}{108}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.3}{2}{In-scope reflects}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.4}{2}{Out-of-scope reflects}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.5}{2}{Attribute relevance}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.6}{2}{Orphan object instances}
\thispagestyle{hla-body-no-ieee}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.035}{69.786}{379.965}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute is a subscribed attribute of the known%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{81.785}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class of the object instance, or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{96.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.036}{96.785}{379.964}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute is a subscribed attribute of the known%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{108.785}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class of the object instance with regions, and the update region set of the instance attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{120.785}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 overlaps the subscription region set of the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute at%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{132.785}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the known class of the instance attribute at the subscribing joined federate.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{156.645}{%
 6.1.3 In-scope reflects%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{180.784}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If an instance attribute is in scope for a given joined federate \textbf{\emph{F}}, exactly one other joined federate exists (\textbf{\emph{U}})%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{192.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in the federation execution that is capable of invoking the \emph{Update Attribute Values} service for that instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{204.784}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute so that if \textbf{\emph{U}} were to invoke the \emph{Update Attribute Values} service for that instance attribute, all of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{216.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 preconditions for the invocation of the corresponding \emph{Reflect Attribute Values \textdagger{}} service at \textbf{\emph{F}} are satisfied.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{240.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The \emph{Reflect Attribute Values \textdagger{}} service may be invoked at a joined federate for a given instance attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{252.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 when%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{270.783}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{270.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The instance attribute is in scope.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{285.782}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{285.782}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A corresponding \emph{Update Attribute Values} service for the instance attribute was invoked by another%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{297.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{321.642}{%
 6.1.4 Out-of-scope reflects%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{345.781}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The \emph{Reflect Attribute Values \textdagger{}} service may also be invoked at a joined federate for a given instance attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{357.781}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 when%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{375.781}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{375.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The instance attribute is out of scope.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{390.781}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{390.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A corresponding \emph{Update Attribute Values} service for the instance attribute was invoked by another%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{402.780}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate when the instance attribute was in scope.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{426.641}{%
 6.1.5 Attribute relevance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{450.780}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate may also direct the RTI, via the \emph{Enable/Disable} \emph{Attribute Relevance Advisory Switch}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{462.779}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 services, to indicate that the joined federate does or does not want the RTI to use the \emph{Turn Updates On For}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{474.779}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Object Instance \textdagger{}} and \emph{Turn Updates Off For Object Instance \textdagger{}} services to inform the joined federate when%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{486.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 updates to particular instance attributes are relevant to the other joined federates in the federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{498.779}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the \emph{Advisories Use Known Class switch }is disabled, the attribute relevance advisories are based on the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{510.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscriptions rather than the known class of the particular instance. This can mean that a federate gets a \emph{Turn}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{522.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Updates On For Object Instance \textdagger{}} even if updates to a particular instance attribute are not reflected by any%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{534.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{558.638}{%
 6.1.6 Orphan object instances%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{582.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An orphan object instance can result from rare conditions where it is unknown by all joined federates and all%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{594.777}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of its instance attributes have become unowned (e.g., because the last joined federate to know the object%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{606.777}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance has resigned or invoked Local Delete Object Instance). Because an orphan object instance is not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{618.777}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known by any joined federate, its attribute instances cannot become owned by any means (i.e., acquiring%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{630.777}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ownership of attributes requires the object instance is known, see preconditions for 7.4, 7.8, and 7.9).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{642.776}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Because all of its attribute instances are unowned, an orphan object instance cannot be discovered or known%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{654.776}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 by any means (i.e., discovery requires that at least one instance attribute is owned by a federate or the RTI,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{666.776}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 see preconditions for 6.9). Consequently, orphan object instances are unreachable by any current or future%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{678.776}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate and the RTI shall delete them.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

