 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{488.686}{%
 6.1.11 Transportation types%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{512.825}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The type of transportation that carries instance attribute values and interactions can be controlled using%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{524.825}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 various HLA facilities. A transportation type shall be defined as either reliable (which means that delivery of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{536.825}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 one copy of the data is guaranteed) or best effort (which means that data may be lost in transport). The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{548.825}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 following transportation types shall always be supported by an RTI:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{563.824}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.973}{563.824}{400.027}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 HLAreliable: which is the default reliable transportation type%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{578.824}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{578.824}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 HLAbestEffort: which is the default best-effort transportation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{602.824}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Other transportation types may be supported by the RTI. If a transportation type is requested by a joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{614.824}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate or in the FDD but not supported by the RTI or other infrastructure components, the RTI may instead%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{626.823}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 fall back to a corresponding (reliable or best-effort) transportation type of its choosing. Ultimately the RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{638.823}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall fallback to the corresponding default transportation type (HLAreliable or HLAbestEffort).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{662.823}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate may request a change of the transportation type for attributes that it owns using the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{674.823}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Request Attribute Transportation Type Change} service. When this operation has completed, the federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{686.823}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall receive an invocation of the \emph{Confirm Attribute Transportation Type Change \textdagger{} }service, specifying the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{698.822}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 transportation type that was actually achieved, which may or may not have changed.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{113}{112}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.12}{2}{Passelization}
\HLAServiceBookmark{6.1.13}{2}{Sending updates with update rate reduction}
\thispagestyle{hla-body-no-ieee}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Similarly, a joined federate may request a change of the transportation type for interactions using the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Request Interaction Transportation Type Change} service. When this operation has completed, the joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate shall receive an invocation of the \emph{Confirm Interaction Transportation Type Change \textdagger{}} service,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{105.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specifying the transportation type that was actually achieved, which may or may not have changed.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{129.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In case the FDD specifies a transportation type that is not available, the RTI shall silently fallback to a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{141.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 corresponding transportation type. It is still possible for a joined federate to inspect the transportation type%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{153.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 employed by using the \emph{Query Attribute Transportation Type} service, which will result in a \emph{Report Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Transportation Type \textdagger{}} service invocation. The corresponding services for interactions are \emph{Query Interaction}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{177.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Transportation Type} and \emph{Report Interaction Transportation Type \textdagger{}}.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{201.644}{%
 6.1.12 Passelization%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{225.783}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 All of the instance attribute/value pairs in an \emph{Update Attribute Values} service invocation for instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{237.783}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attributes that have identical transportation type, sent message order type, and set of sent region designators%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{249.783}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (if present) shall be defined as one passel. The instance attributes that make up a passel shall be available for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{261.783}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 delivery in the same \emph{Reflect Attribute Values} service invocation. The delivery of the instance attributes that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{273.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 make up the passel shall depend on the subscriptions and subscription region specifications at the reflecting%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{285.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate. Elements shall not change passels, passels shall not be divided, and passels shall not be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{297.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 combined with other passels. Since one \emph{Update Attribute Values} service invocation may result in the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{309.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 creation of multiple passels (where sent transportation type, sent message order type, and set of sent region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{321.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 designators are different), an \emph{Update Attribute Values} service invocation may result in multiple \emph{Reflect}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{333.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Values} service invocations in a reflecting joined federate. Instance attributes delivered via a \emph{Reflect}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{345.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Values} service invocation shall not contain elements from more than one \emph{Update Attribute Values}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{357.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service invocation.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{381.641}{%
 6.1.13 Sending updates with update rate reduction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{405.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall not provide an update rate to a joined federate that exceeds the subscribed update rate. It shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{417.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 not, however, deliver any more updates than what is provided by the owning joined federate. In other words,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{429.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 any minimum update rate shall not be guaranteed. In case a joined federate has subscribed with an update%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{441.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 rate other than the default update rate, the RTI shall handle this situation as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.018}{456.780}{421.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.972}{456.780}{400.028}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For attributes with best-effort transportation, messages shall not be delivered to a joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{468.779}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 with an update rate higher than the subscribed update rate. Any messages in excess of this rate shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{480.779}{400.023}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be dropped. Given a maximum update rate of \emph{x} Hz and given that a message has been delivered at%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{492.779}{400.023}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 wall-clock time \emph{t}, no message shall be delivered before \emph{t} + (1 / \emph{x}).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.016}{507.779}{421.984}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.976}{507.779}{400.024}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For attributes with reliable transportation, no messages shall be dropped.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{531.778}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In case the attribute relevancy advisory switch is enabled, the owning joined federate shall be notified of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{543.778}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 maximum actively subscribed update rate as part of the \emph{Turn Updates On For Object Instance \textdagger{}} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{555.778}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation. The \emph{Turn Updates On for Object Instance \textdagger{}} service invocation shall also be invoked at owning%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{567.778}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federates whenever the maximum actively subscribed update rate in the federation execution changes.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{579.778}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In case any joined federate is actively subscribed using the default update rate, no update rate designator will%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{591.777}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be provided as part of the \emph{Turn Updates On for Object Instance \textdagger{}} service invocation. In case the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{603.777}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 transportation type for an attribute is changed, the update rate reduction behavior for the new transportation%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{615.777}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 type shall apply.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{639.777}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If operating in a synchronous callback model, a subscribing joined federate whose rate of invoking the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.996}{651.776}{432.004}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Evoke Callback} service (\emph{Re}) and rate of updates by the publishing joined federate (\emph{Rp}) are higher than the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{663.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscribed update rate (\emph{Rs}), then the RTI shall drop messages at a rate of \emph{Rp}--\emph{Rs}. If either \emph{Re} or \emph{Rp} is less%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{675.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 than \emph{Rs}, there are no guarantees on the rate of messages received by the subscribing joined federate.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
