 \HLAServiceHeadingAt{119.363}{%
 6.8 \emph{Register Object Instance} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{144.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall create a federation execution-wide unique object instance handle and shall coadunate that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{155.766}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 handle with an instance of the supplied object class. All instance attributes of the object instance for which%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{166.805}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the corresponding class attributes are currently published by the registering joined federate shall be set as%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 owned by the registering joined federate.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{198.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An object instance handle shall be uniform throughout the federation execution; i.e., with respect to a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{209.765}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 particular object instance, the handle provided to the joined federate that registers the object instance shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{220.804}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be the same handle provided to all joined federates that discover the object instance. The phrase “the same%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{231.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 handle” shall denote handle equality rather than handle identity. Two handles shall be considered to be the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{242.764}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 same if, according to the comparison operator in each of the APIs (for example, according to the “equals”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{253.804}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 method in the Java API), the handles would be determined to be equal. The handles shall also have equality%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{264.784}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 between joined federates that are using different language APIs. The handles may be communicated%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{275.764}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 between joined federates via instance attributes or interaction parameters.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{296.763}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the optional object instance name argument is supplied, that name shall have been successfully reserved%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{307.803}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 by the registering federate as indicated by the \emph{Object Instance Name Reserved \textdagger{} }service or the \emph{Multiple}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{318.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Object Instance Names Reserved \textdagger{}} service and shall be coadunated with the object instance. If the optional%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{329.763}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 object instance name argument is not supplied, the RTI shall create a federation execution-wide unique%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{340.803}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 name, and that name shall be coadunated with the object instance.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{361.663}{%
