 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{262.806}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The \emph{Reflect Attribute Values \textdagger{} }service shall provide the joined federate with new values for the specified%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{274.805}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attributes. This service, coupled with the \emph{Update Attribute Values} service, forms the primary data%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{286.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 exchange mechanism supported by the RTI.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{310.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The user-supplied tag argument supplied to the corresponding \emph{Update Attribute Values} service invocation%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{322.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be provided with all corresponding \emph{Reflect Attribute Value \textdagger{} }service invocations, even multiple ones in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{334.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the same reflecting joined federate.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{358.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The transportation type shall indicate the transportation type of the passel associated with this service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{370.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{394.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A timestamp shall be provided if one was specified in the corresponding \emph{Update Attribute Values} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{406.803}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation. The receive message order type shall indicate the type (either RO or TSO) of the received%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{418.803}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 message. The timestamp and receive message order type arguments shall be supplied together or not at all.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{430.803}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The sent message order type shall indicate the type (either RO or TSO) of the sent message.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{454.803}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A retraction handle shall be provided if and only if the sent message order type is TSO.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{478.802}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If specified instance attributes have available dimensions and the Convey Region Designator Sets Switch for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{490.802}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 this joined federate is enabled, the Set of Sent Region Designators argument shall contain a copy of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{502.802}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 update region realization (see 9.1.7), if any, that was used for update of the instance attributes at the joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{514.802}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate, which invoked the corresponding \emph{Update Attribute Values} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{538.801}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The producing joined federate argument shall contain the designator for the joined federate that updated.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{562.801}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate invoking the \emph{Update Attribute Values} service shall not receive the induced \emph{Reflect}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{574.801}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Values \textdagger{}} service invocation, regardless of the subscription situation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{598.800}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The \emph{Reflect Attribute Values \textdagger{} }service call shall follow passelization requirements (see 6.1.12).%
 }
