\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{69.646}{%
 \textbf{7.1.1 Ownership and publication}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The ownership of an instance attribute is closely related to whether that instance attribute’s corresponding%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class attribute is published at the known class of the instance attribute. In other words, the ownership state%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{117.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 machine in Figure 16, which operates in parallel with the publication state machine in Figure 11, also shares%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{129.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interdependencies with the publication state machine. A joined federate shall be publishing a class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{141.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 at the known class of an object instance in order to own the corresponding instance attribute of that object%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{153.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance. Therefore, the following are true:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{165.784}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.963}{165.784}{400.037}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate shall be publishing a class attribute at the known class of an object instance before%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{177.784}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 it may become the owner of the corresponding instance attribute of that object instance. This%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{189.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interdependency between ownership and publication is expressed in Figure 16 by the Not Able to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{201.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Acquire state, the [in “Unpublished (\emph{i}, \emph{j})”] and [in “Published (\emph{i}, \emph{j})”] transitions in the Unowned%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{213.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) state, and the conditional transition into the Owned (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) and Unowned (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) states from%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{225.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the start state.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{237.783}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{237.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the joined federate that owns an instance attribute stops publishing the corresponding class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{249.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute at the known class of the instance attribute, the instance attribute shall immediately become%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{261.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unowned. This interdependency between ownership and publication is expressed in Figure 16 by the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{273.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 transition from the Owned (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) state to the Unowned (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) state that is labeled [in “Unpublished%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{285.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (\emph{i}, \emph{j})”]. As depicted by the guard on the transition from the Published (\emph{i}, \emph{j}) state to the Unpublished%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{297.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (\emph{i}, \emph{j}) state in the publication state machine shown in Figure 11, a joined federate shall not stop%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{309.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 publication of a class attribute at a given class if there is an object instance that has that class as its%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{321.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known class and that has a corresponding instance attribute that is in either the Acquisition Pending%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{333.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 or Willing to Acquire (\emph{i}, \emph{k}, \emph{j}) state at that joined federate. In other words, a joined federate shall not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{345.781}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 stop publishing a class attribute at a given class if there is an object instance that has that class as its%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{357.781}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known class and that has a corresponding instance attribute for which the joined federate has%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{369.781}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invoked the following:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{384.781}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{384.786}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service, but has not yet received an invocation of the \emph{Confirm}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{396.785}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition Cancellation \textdagger{}} service, the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{144.480}{408.785}{377.520}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{\textdagger{} }service, or the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{423.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{423.785}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available} service, but has not yet received an invocation of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{435.785}{379.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service, received an invocation of the \emph{Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{447.785}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service, or invoked the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{459.784}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{service} [after which condition 1) (above) applies].%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{483.645}{%
 \textbf{7.1.2 Ownership transfer}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{507.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An instance attribute that is successfully divested shall become unowned by the divesting joined federate. If%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{519.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 an instance attribute is unowned, its corresponding class attribute at the known class of the instance attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{531.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 may be either published or unpublished. If the class attribute is published at that class, the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{543.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be eligible to acquire the corresponding instance attribute, and it may be offered ownership of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{555.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute by the RTI via the \emph{Request Attribute Ownership Assumption \textdagger{}} service. There are five ways%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{567.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in which an owning joined federate may attempt to divest itself of an instance attribute and two ways in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{579.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 which a non-owning joined federate may attempt to acquire one.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{603.643}{%
 \textbf{7.1.2.1 Divestiture}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{627.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The five actions that a joined federate may take to cause an instance attribute that it owns to become%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{639.781}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unowned are as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{651.781}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{651.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may invoke the \emph{Unconditional Attribute Ownership Divestiture} service, in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{663.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 which case, the instance attribute shall immediately become unowned by that joined federate and, in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{675.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 fact, by all joined federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{687.781}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{687.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may invoke the \emph{Negotiated Attribute Ownership Divestiture} service, which%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{699.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 notifies the RTI that the joined federate wishes to divest itself of the instance attribute, providing that%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{152}{151}
\HLAServiceBookmark{7.1.2}{2}{Ownership transfer mechanisms}
\HLAServiceBookmark{7.1.2.1}{3}{Divestiture}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the RTI can locate a joined federate that is willing to own the instance attribute. If any joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{81.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates are in the process of trying to acquire the instance attribute, these joined federates are%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{93.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 willing to own the instance attribute. The RTI can try to identify other joined federates that are%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{105.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 willing to own the instance attribute by invoking the \emph{Request Attribute Ownership Assumption \textdagger{}}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{117.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service at all joined federates that are not in the process of trying to acquire the instance attribute, but%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{129.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that are publishing the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute at the publishing joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{141.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate’s known class of the instance attribute. If the RTI is able to locate a joined federate that is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{153.784}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 willing to acquire the instance attribute, the RTI shall notify the divesting joined federate by%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{165.784}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invoking the \emph{Request Divestiture Confirmation \textdagger{}} service. The divesting joined federate may then%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{177.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 complete the negotiated divestiture using the \emph{Confirm Divestiture} service, which causes ownership%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{189.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of the instance attribute to be lost.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{201.784}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{201.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may invoke the \emph{Attribute Ownership Divestiture If Wanted} service, which%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{213.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 notifies the RTI that the joined federate wishes to divest itself of ownership of the instance attribute,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{225.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 providing that another joined federate is attempting to acquire ownership of it. This service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{237.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation has a return argument that the RTI shall use to indicate the set of instance attributes for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{249.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 which the joined federate has divested ownership. If an instance attribute is not in the returned%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{261.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute set, it was not divested, and the request to divest this instance attribute shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{273.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 concluded. If the \emph{Attribute Ownership Divestiture If Wanted} service returns with the designated%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{285.782}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute among the set of released instance attributes, the instance attribute shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{297.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unowned by the invoking joined federate. [In Figure 16, the transition from the owned to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{309.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unowned state via an \emph{Attribute Ownership Divestiture If Wanted }service invocation is labeled%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{321.782}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 “\emph{Attribute Ownership Divestiture If Wanted} (ret: divested).” This is a convenience notation%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{333.782}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 indicating that the instance attribute in question is a member of the returned instance attribute set.]%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{345.781}{421.977}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{345.781}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may stop publishing the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute at the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{357.781}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known class of the instance attribute; this step shall result in the instance attribute immediately%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{369.781}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 becoming unowned by that joined federate and, in fact, by all joined federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{381.781}{421.977}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 e)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{381.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may resign from the federation execution. When a joined federate successfully%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{393.781}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 resigns from the federation execution with the Unconditionally Divest Attributes option, all of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{405.780}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attributes that are owned by that joined federate shall become unowned by that joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{417.780}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate and, in fact, by all joined federates. This transition is not depicted in Figure 16 because it%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{429.780}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 occurs at a joined federate, rather than at an instance attribute, level of operation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{453.780}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Of the five ways a joined federate may divest itself of an instance attribute, only the \emph{Negotiated Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{465.780}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Divestiture} service may be canceled. A \emph{Negotiated Attribute Ownership Divestiture} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{477.779}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation shall remain pending until either the instance attribute becomes unowned or the divesting joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{489.779}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate cancels the divestiture request by invoking the \emph{Cancel Negotiated Attribute Ownership Divestiture}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{501.779}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service. Cancellation of the divestiture shall be guaranteed to be successful.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{525.779}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Of the five ways a joined federate may divest itself of an instance attribute, three ways (invocation of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{537.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Unconditional Attribute Ownership Divestiture} service, a request to stop publication of the instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{549.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute’s corresponding class attribute at the known class of the instance attribute, and invocation of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{561.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Resign Federation Execution} service) shall result in the instance attribute becoming unowned by all joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{573.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates. When either the \emph{Negotiated Attribute Ownership Divestiture} or the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{585.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Divestiture If Wanted} service is used, the RTI shall guarantee that immediately after the owning joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{597.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate loses ownership of the instance attribute, another joined federate shall be granted ownership of it.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{609.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For purposes of determining an instance attribute’s scope, the instance attribute shall be considered to be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{621.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 continuously owned during its transfer of ownership from the divesting joined federate to the acquiring%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{633.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate via either the \emph{Negotiated Attribute Ownership Divestiture} or the\emph{ Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{645.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Divestiture If Wanted} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{669.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the value of an instance attribute is being updated by a joined federate using TSO messages and that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{681.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate is initiating a negotiated divestiture of that instance attribute, the divesting and receiving%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{693.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federates should be aware of potential causality or reflection anomalies. %
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{153}{152}
\HLAServiceBookmark{7.1.2.2}{3}{Acquisition}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Because the divestiture is not associated with a timestamp, the time position of the receiving joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 at which ownership of the instance attribute is acquired may be earlier or later than that of the divesting%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate, giving either a gap or an overlap in the time intervals on the time axis for which the joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates own the instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Some issues to consider are as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{149.764}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.968}{149.764}{400.032}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There may be points on the time axis at which neither joined federate owns the instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{161.764}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 This situation may result in an interval of timestamps for which no updates to the value of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{173.764}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute are provided, unless special steps are taken by one or both of the joined federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{185.764}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{185.764}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There may be points on the time axis at which both joined federates own the instance attribute. This%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{197.764}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 situation may result in updates to the value of the instance attribute being produced by both joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{209.764}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates that contain the same timestamp, unless special steps are taken by one or both of the joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{221.763}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{233.763}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.973}{233.763}{400.027}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There may be TSO updates sent by the divesting joined federate that have not been delivered to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{245.763}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 other joined federates (i.e., they are queued in the RTI) when the divestiture occurs. Some of these%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{257.763}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 outstanding TSO updates may be retractable by the divesting joined federate; others may not be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{269.763}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 retractable. See restrictions in 8.22 for details.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{281.762}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{281.762}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There may be additional information that the divesting joined federate needs to transfer along with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{293.762}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ownership of the instance attribute. %
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{317.622}{%
 \textbf{7.1.2.2 Acquisition}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{341.761}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall provide both of the following two ways for a joined federate that is publishing a class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{353.761}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 at a given class to acquire an analogous instance attribute of an object instance that has that class as the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{365.761}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 known class at the joined federate attempting to acquire the attribute:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{385.801}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.972}{385.801}{400.028}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may invoke the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service, which shall inform the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{397.800}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 RTI that it shall invoke the \emph{Request Attribute Ownership Release \textdagger{}} service at the joined federate that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{409.800}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 owns the designated instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{421.800}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{421.800}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate may invoke the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available} service, which%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{433.800}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall inform the RTI that it wants to acquire the designated instance attribute only if it is already%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{445.800}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unowned by all joined federates or if it is in the process of being divested by its owner.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{469.799}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The first method of acquisition can be thought of as an intrusive acquisition because the RTI will notify the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{481.799}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate that owns the instance attribute that another joined federate wants to acquire it and request%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{493.799}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that the owning joined federate release the instance attribute for acquisition by the requesting joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{505.799}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate. The second method of acquisition can be thought of as a nonintrusive acquisition because the RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{517.799}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 will not notify the owning joined federate of the request to acquire the instance attribute. The \emph{Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{529.798}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Acquisition} service can also be thought of as taking precedence over the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{541.798}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition If Available} service. A joined federate that has invoked the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{553.798}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service and is in the Acquisition Pending state shall not invoke the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{565.798}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Available} service. If a joined federate that has invoked the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{577.798}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service and is in the Willing to Acquire state invokes the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service, that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{589.797}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate shall enter the Acquisition Pending state.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{613.797}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service invocation may be explicitly canceled, but an \emph{Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{625.797}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Acquisition If Available }service invocation may not be explicitly canceled. When a joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{637.797}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate invokes the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available }service, either the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{649.796}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service or the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service shall be invoked at that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{661.796}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate in response. If the instance attribute is unowned by all joined federates (and no other joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{673.796}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate is attempting to acquire it), the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{685.796}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invoked. If the joined federate is in the Not Divesting state with respect to the instance attribute, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{697.796}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service shall be invoked. Otherwise, either the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{154}{153}
\HLAServiceBookmark{7.1.3}{2}{Privilege to delete object}
\HLAServiceBookmark{7.1.4}{2}{User-supplied tags}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service or the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service may be invoked,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 depending on what service, if any, the owning joined federate invokes.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a joined federate invokes the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service invocation, on the other hand,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 this request shall remain pending until the instance attribute is acquired (as indicated by an invocation of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service), acquisition of the instance attribute is denied (as%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 indicated by an invocation of the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service), or the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{153.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 successfully cancels the acquisition request. A joined federate may attempt to cancel the acquisition request%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{165.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 by invoking the \emph{Cancel Attribute Ownership Acquisition }service. The \emph{Cancel Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{177.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition }service is not guaranteed to be successful. If it is successful, the RTI shall indicate this success to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{189.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the canceling joined federate by invoking the \emph{Confirm Attribute Ownership Acquisition Cancellation \textdagger{}}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{201.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service. If it fails, the RTI shall indicate this failure to the canceling joined federate by invoking the \emph{Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{213.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service, thereby granting ownership of the instance attribute to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{225.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{249.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service invocation shall override an \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{261.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Available }service invocation. In other words, a joined federate that has invoked the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{273.783}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition If Available }service may, before it receives an invocation of either the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{285.782}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition Notification \textdagger{}} service or the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service, invoke the \emph{Attribute}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{297.782}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Ownership Acquisition} service. In this case, the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available }service request%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{309.782}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be implicitly canceled, and the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition} service request shall remain pending%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{321.782}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 until the instance attribute is acquired, acquisition of the instance attribute is denied, or the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{333.782}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 successfully cancels the acquisition request. A joined federate that has invoked the \emph{Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{345.781}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition} service, but has not yet received an invocation of the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{357.781}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Notification \textdagger{}} service, the \emph{Attribute Ownership Unavailable \textdagger{}} service, or the \emph{Confirm Attribute Ownership}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{369.781}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Acquisition Cancellation \textdagger{} }service, shall not invoke the \emph{Attribute Ownership Acquisition If Available}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{381.781}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{405.641}{%
 \textbf{7.1.3 Privilege to delete object}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{429.780}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 All object classes shall have an available attribute called \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject}. As with all other%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{441.780}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 available attributes, a joined federate shall be publishing the \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{453.780}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 at the known class of an object instance in order to be eligible for ownership of a corresponding%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{465.780}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{489.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} instance attribute shall be transferable among joined federates. All%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{501.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ownership management services for \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} instance attributes shall act the same as%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{513.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 they are for all other instance attributes. The reason that a joined federate may want to own the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{525.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} instance attribute, however, is different. Ownership of a typical instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{537.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute shall give a joined federate the privilege to provide new values for that instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{549.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Ownership of the \textbf{HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject} instance attribute of an object instance shall give the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{561.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate the additional right to delete that object instance from the federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{585.646}{%
 \textbf{7.1.4 User-supplied tags}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{609.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Several of the ownership management services take a user-supplied tag as an argument. These arguments%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{621.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be provided as a mechanism for conducting information between joined federates that could be used to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{633.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 implement priority or other schemes. Although the content and use of these tags are outside of the scope of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{645.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 this specification, the RTI shall pass these user-supplied tags from joined federates that are trying to acquire%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{657.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 an instance attribute to the joined federate that owns the instance attribute and from the joined federate that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{669.784}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 is trying to divest itself of an instance attribute to the joined federates that are able to acquire the instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{681.784}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute. In particular, the following apply: %
 }
