 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 timestamp was supplied in the service invocation that sends the message. Table 2 illustrates how the order%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 type of a sent message shall be determined.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Table 3 illustrates how the order type of a received message shall be determined. The order type of a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 received message shall be determined by whether that joined federate is time-constrained and by the order%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 type of the corresponding sent message. As shown in these two tables, a message retraction designator is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 provided to both the sender and the receiver if the sent message order type is TSO, regardless of the order%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 type of the received message.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Because of the above rule defining the order type of a received message, the RTI shall sometimes convert a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{189.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 sent TSO message to a received RO message at some receiving joined federates. The need for such%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{201.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 conversions shall be considered on a per-joined-federate basis. Thus, the received messages at different%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{213.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federates that correspond to the same sent message may be of different order types. Sent RO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{225.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 messages shall never be converted to received TSO messages.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{249.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Except when the \emph{Flush Queue Request} service is used, messages that are received as TSO messages shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{261.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 received only by a given joined federate in TSO, regardless of the joined federates from which the messages%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{273.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 originate and regardless of the sequence in which the messages were sent. Thus, two TSO messages with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{285.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 different timestamps shall always be received by each joined federate in the same order. Multiple TSO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{297.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 messages having the same timestamp may be received in an indeterminate order.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{321.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Messages that are received as RO messages shall be received in an arbitrary order. A timestamp shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{333.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 provided with the received message if one was specified when the message was sent. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{213.781}{367.662}{308.219}{\sffamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
