 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{69.646}{%
 \textbf{8.1.5 Time-regulating joined federates}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Only time-regulating joined federates may send TSO messages. A joined federate shall request to become%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 time-regulating by invoking the \emph{Enable Time Regulation} service. The RTI shall subsequently make the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate time-regulating by invoking the \emph{Time Regulation Enabled \textdagger{}} service at that joined federate. A%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{129.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate shall cease to be time-regulating whenever it invokes the \emph{Disable Time Regulation} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{153.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Each time-regulating joined federate shall provide a lookahead when becoming time-regulating. Lookahead%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{165.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be a logical time interval that establishes the lowest value of timestamps that can be sent in TSO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{177.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 messages by the joined federate. Specifically, a time-regulating joined federate shall not send a TSO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{189.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 message that contains a timestamp less than its current logical time plus its current lookahead. Once%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{201.784}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 established, changes to a joined federate’s lookahead may be requested only by using the \emph{Modify Lookahead}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{213.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{237.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A time-regulating joined federate with a lookahead of zero shall be subject to an additional restriction. If%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{249.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 such a joined federate has advanced its logical time by use of \emph{Time Advance Request} or \emph{Next Message}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{261.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Request} service, it shall not send TSO messages that contain timestamps less than or equal to its logical time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{273.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (plus its lookahead, which is zero), rather than the usual less-than restriction. Subsequent use of a time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{285.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 advancement service that moves the joined federate’s logical time forward lifts this additional restriction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{297.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (and imposes the restriction of the subsequent advancement service). For example, if a zero lookahead%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{309.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate were to invoke \emph{Time Advance Request} service (\emph{t}{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont 1}) and to follow this step with an invocation%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{321.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of \emph{Time Advance Request Available} service (\emph{t}{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont 1}), that joined federate would still have the additional%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{333.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 restriction. After the \emph{Time Advance Request Available} service is granted, it still may not send any TSO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{345.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 messages with a timestamp less than or equal to \emph{t}{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont 1} (the \emph{Time Advance Request} restriction) because the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{357.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 second advance did not advance the joined federate’s logical time.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{381.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A time-regulating joined federate that has advanced its logical time via the \emph{Flush Queue Grant \textdagger{} }service as a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{393.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 result of using the \emph{Flush Queue Request} service shall be further restricted from sending a TSO message with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{405.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a timestamp less than its optimistic logical time plus the lookahead it would have if granted to the optimistic%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{417.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 logical time. The lookahead the federate would have if actually granted to the optimistic logical time is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{429.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 referred to as the optimistic lookahead (OL).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{453.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A time-regulating joined federate need not send TSO messages in TSO, but all TSO messages that it sends%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{465.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be received by other joined federates in timestamped order (if they are received as TSO messages)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{477.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 except when the \emph{Flush Queue Request} service is used.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{501.644}{%
 \textbf{8.1.6 Time-constrained joined federates}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{525.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Only time-constrained joined federates can receive messages as TSO messages. A joined federate shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{537.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 request to become time-constrained by invoking the \emph{Enable Time Constrained} service. The RTI shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{549.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subsequently make the joined federate time-constrained by invoking the \emph{Time Constrained Enabled \textdagger{}}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{561.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service at that joined federate. A joined federate shall cease to be time-constrained whenever it invokes the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{573.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Disable Time Constrained} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{597.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In order to ensure that a time-constrained joined federate shall never receive a TSO message with a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{609.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 timestamp less than its logical time, a bound is placed on each time-constrained joined federate that limits%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{621.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 how far it can advance its logical time. The bound ensures that a time-constrained joined federate cannot%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{633.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 advance its logical time past a point at which TSO messages could still be sent by another joined federate. If%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{645.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a time-constrained joined federate request to advance its logical time beyond its bound, the time advance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{657.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall not be granted until its bound has increased beyond the logical time to be granted.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{681.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 This bound on advancement is expressed in terms of a value called the Greatest Available Logical Time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{693.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (GALT). Each joined federate shall have a GALT that expresses the greatest logical time to which the RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{705.780}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 guarantees it can grant an advance without having to wait for other joined federates to advance. In the case%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
