\HLASourcePage{184}{183}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of some time advance services (\emph{Time Advance Request} and \emph{Next Message Request}) the joined federate shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 be granted only to logical times that are less than its GALT. In the case of other time advance services (\emph{Time}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{93.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Advance Request Available}, \emph{Next Message Request Available}, and \emph{Flush Queue Request}), the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{105.785}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be granted only to logical times that are less than or equal to its GALT.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{129.785}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate’s GALT is calculated by the RTI and is based on factors such as:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.018}{144.784}{421.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{144.784}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate’s smallest timestamp of TSO messages delivered since the last time advance.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.018}{159.784}{421.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{159.784}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate’s smallest timestamp of messages not yet delivered (e.g., those in the TSO%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{171.784}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 queue or in transit).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.018}{186.784}{421.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{186.784}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The temporal state of the other time-regulating joined federates including logical time, lookahead,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{198.784}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and requests to advance logical time.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{222.783}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 However, if there are no other time-regulating joined federates in the execution, the joined federate’s GALT%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{234.783}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 is unregulated and its value is undefined. When the GALT is undefined, the behavior of the time advancing%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{246.783}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 services (see Table 1) shall be determined by the value of the Non-Regulated-Grant (NRG) switch.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{261.783}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{261.783}{400.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the NRG switch is enabled, an undefined GALT indicates that the bound on advancement is such%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{273.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that a time-constrained joined federate may advance to any point without having to wait for another%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{285.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate to advance.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{300.782}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{300.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If the NRG switch is disabled, an undefined GALT indicates that a time-constrained joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{312.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 will not be granted to a time greater than its current logical time.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{336.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There are degenerate states that can occur both when the NRG switch is enabled and when it is disabled.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{360.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the NRG switch is enabled and there are no other time-regulating joined federates, a time-constrained%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{372.781}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate may advance unregulated. If federates are not synchronized, this allowance can result in a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{384.781}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 runaway federate situation where the first federate to join can advance time into the far future before another%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{396.780}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate joins. A runaway federate may also come about if the only time-regulating joined federate in a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{408.780}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federation execution disables time regulation, resigns, or suffers a fault condition.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{432.780}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When the NRG switch is disabled and there is a single time-regulating and time-constrained joined federate,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.997}{444.780}{432.003}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 then this federate will not be able to advance because it is time-constrained and there are no other regulators.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{456.780}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Further, any other time-constrained joined federates will not be able to advance because the time-regulating%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{468.779}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and time-constrained joined federate cannot advance.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{492.779}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Federates should take care to either avoid or react to these degenerate cases through the employment of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{504.779}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 synchronization points and fault tolerance services.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{528.778}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 While GALT is used only by the RTI to bound the advancement of time-constrained joined federates,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{540.778}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 nonconstrained joined federates also have a GALT. For a nonconstrained joined federate, GALT expresses%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{552.778}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the bound that would apply to that joined federate if it were to become time-constrained.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{576.778}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Each joined federate shall have another value that builds on the idea of GALT called Least Incoming%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{588.777}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Timestamp (LITS). A joined federate’s LITS shall express the smallest timestamp that the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{600.777}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 could (but not necessarily will) receive in the future in a TSO message. A joined federate’s LITS is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{612.777}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 calculated by the RTI and is based on the joined federate’s GALT and any queued TSO messages that may%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{624.777}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 later be received by the joined federate. If the joined federate’s GALT is undefined and there are no queued%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{636.777}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 TSO messages that the joined federate could receive, the joined federate’s LITS shall also be undefined.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{185}{184}
\HLAServiceBookmark{8.1.5}{2}{Time-advance grants}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedRule{90.780}{692.760}{0.240}{0.35}
 \HLAFixedRule{90.780}{693.240}{0.240}{0.35}
