 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{430.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the logical time of the joined federate has been advanced to this value. The OLT is the minimum of the time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{442.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 supplied in the \emph{Flush Queue Request} and the timestamps of any TSO messages delivered in response to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{454.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Flush Queue Request}. It indicates the logical time that the joined federate would have been granted if the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{466.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 RTI could have guaranteed that no other TSO messages with a timestamp less than it would be received in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{478.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the future. In other words, the RTI’s generation of the OLT optimistically assumes that even though there%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{490.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 could be TSO messages in transit or yet to be sent, none of these TSO messages will have a timestamp less%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{502.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 than the OLT.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{526.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall guarantee that no additional TSO messages shall be delivered in the future with timestamps%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{538.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 less than the logical time value of the grant.%
 }
