 \HLAServiceHeadingAt{276.383}{%
 \textbf{8.25 }\textbf{\emph{Change Default Attribute Order Type}}\textbf{ service}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{301.806}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Upon a federate gaining ownership of an instance attribute (either through registration or ownership%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{313.805}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 transfer), the instance attribute's order type shall be initialized using the federate’s corresponding class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{325.805}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute default order type. For each federate when joining, a class attribute's default order type shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{337.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 initialized from the corresponding class attribute description in the current FDD. A joined federate during%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{349.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 execution may choose to change its class attribute's default order type. When changing a default order type,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{361.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a class attribute shall be specified using a class handle for which the class attribute is available along with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{373.805}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the class attribute’s handle. Invoking the Change Default Attribute Order Type service on a class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{385.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall affect the order type of a federate’s future instance attributes of the class attribute irrespective of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{397.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 object class used in the invocation. Existing owned object instances will not change their current order type%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{409.804}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 nor will the class attribute default order type of other federates. %
 }
