\HLASourcePage{217}{216}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1}{1}{Overview}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.1}{2}{Definitions for DDM}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.120}{432.000}{\sffamily\raggedright}{12.00}{12.00}{%
 \textbf{9. Data distribution management (DDM)}%
 }
 \HLAServiceHeadingAt{97.403}{%
 \textbf{9.1 Overview}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{120.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 DDM services may be used by joined federates to reduce both the transmission and the reception of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{131.766}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 irrelevant data. Whereas DM services provide information on data relevance at the class attribute level,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{142.805}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 DDM services add the capability to further refine the data requirements at the instance attribute level.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{153.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Similarly, whereas DM services provide information on data relevance at the interaction class level, DDM%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{164.765}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 services add the capability to further refine the data requirements at the specific interaction level. Producers%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{175.805}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and consumers of data communicated between joined federates may use the DDM services to bound the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{186.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 relevance of such communicated data. As a result, the RTI can help recognize the irrelevant data and reduce%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{197.765}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 its delivery to consumers. The relevance of communicating interactions or instance attribute updates is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{208.804}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 expressed by giving a bounding for relevant communication in a space of user-defined dimensions. Both%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{219.784}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 consumers and producers specify the upper and lower bounds for the relevant portion of that space, and the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{230.764}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 overlap of producers’ and consumers’ region sets is used to bound relevant communication.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{253.665}{%
 \textbf{9.1.1 Definitions for DDM}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{277.804}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The DDM services shall be based on the following concepts and terms:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{292.804}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{292.804}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{dimension} shall be a named interval of nonnegative integers. The interval shall be defined by an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{303.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ordered pair of values. The first value is 0 (zero) for every dimension. The second value, which can%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{314.764}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 vary for each dimension, is that dimension’s upper bound as specified in the FDD.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{325.803}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{325.803}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{range} shall be a continuous semi-open interval on a dimension. The interval is defined by an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{337.803}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ordered pair of values. The first component of the pair shall be called \textbf{range lower bound}, and the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{349.803}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 second component shall be called \textbf{range upper bound}. The range upper bound shall be strictly%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{361.803}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 greater than the range lower bound. The minimum possible difference between a range lower bound%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{373.803}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and a range upper bound shall be 1 (one).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{385.802}{421.977}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{385.802}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{region specification} shall be a set of ranges. The dimensions contained in a region specification%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{397.802}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall be the dimensions of the ranges that are included in the region specification. A region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{409.802}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification shall contain at most one range for any given dimension. Each range in a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{421.802}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification shall be defined in terms of the bounds [0, the corresponding dimension’s upper%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{433.802}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 bound). %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{445.802}{421.977}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{445.802}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{region template} shall be an incomplete region specification where one or more dimensions have%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{457.801}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 not been assigned ranges.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.023}{469.801}{421.977}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 e)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{469.801}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A \textbf{region realization} shall be a region specification that is associated with an instance attribute for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{481.801}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 update, with a sent interaction or with a class attribute or interaction class for subscription. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{493.801}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 generic term \textbf{region} may be used in circumstances where a region specification, a region realization,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{505.801}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 or both apply.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.024}{517.800}{421.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 f)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.961}{517.800}{400.039}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The RTI shall provide the \textbf{default region}, which is defined as having the range [0, the range’s%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{529.800}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimension’s upper bound) for each dimension found in the FDD. The default region shall have all%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{541.800}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimensions found in the FDD, regardless of the class attribute or interaction class with which it is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{553.800}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 associated. The default region realization shall not have a region specification. There shall be no%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{565.800}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 way for a joined federate to refer to the default region. If a joined federate creates a region that has as%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{577.799}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 its dimensions all dimensions found in the FDD and has the range [0, the range’s dimension’s upper%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{589.799}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 bound) for each dimension, this region shall be equivalent to the default region, but it is not the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{601.799}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 default region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.024}{613.799}{421.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 g)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{613.799}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A collection of attribute designator set and region designator set pairs shall be interpreted as a set of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{625.799}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (attribute designator, region designator) pairs. The interpreted form can be viewed as if constructed%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{637.798}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in the following manner:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{652.798}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.031}{652.798}{379.969}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The interpreted form begins as an empty set of (attribute designator, region designator) pairs.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{667.798}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.040}{667.798}{379.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For each pair (of sets) in the attribute designator set and region designator set pair collection,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.024}{679.798}{379.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 create the cross product of the attribute designator set with its region designator set. The result%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.024}{691.798}{379.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 is a collection of (attribute designator, region designator) pairs. The union of all such (attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.024}{703.797}{379.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 designator, region designator) pairs shall be the interpreted form.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{218}{217}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.2}{2}{Relating region specifications and region realizations}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Some DDM services require that the region designator used as an argument shall explicitly be the designator%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of a region specification. Whereas other DDM services require that the region designator used as an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{93.785}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 argument be the designator of either a region specification, or a region template. For example, the Commit%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Region Modifications service requires that the region designator used as an argument be either a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification, or a region template that has had the Set Range Bounds service called at least once for all of its%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimensions. If a DDM or Support service is invoked with a region designator argument that is not of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{141.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 variety it is expecting, the service shall throw the “Invalid region” exception. Hence, the circumstances that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 shall cause the “Invalid region” exception to be thrown vary from service to service, depending on the type%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of region entity (template, specification, or template with all range bounds set) for which the service is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 expected to receive a designator. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{201.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For all services that can be used to create a region realization from a region specification, the region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{213.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 designator argument shall be the designator of a region specification. Specifically, the following services,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{225.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 which result in the creation of region realizations from region specifications, require that the region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{237.783}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 designator argument be the designator of a region specification: \emph{Register Object Instance With Regions},%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{249.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Associate Regions For Updates}, \emph{Subscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions}, \emph{Subscribe Interaction}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{261.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Class With Regions}, \emph{Send Interaction With Regions}, and \emph{Request Attribute Value Update With Regions}.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{285.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following services also require that the region designator argument be the designator of a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{297.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification: \emph{Unassociate Regions for Updates}, \emph{Unsubscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions}, and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{309.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Unsubscribe Interaction Class With Regions}.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{333.782}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The region designator argument for the \emph{Delete Region} service shall be the designator of either a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{345.781}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 template or a region specification. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{369.781}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There are also three Support services that take a region designator as argument:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{384.781}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{384.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The region designator argument for the \emph{Get Range Bounds} service shall be the designator of either a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{396.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region specification or a region realization.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{411.780}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{411.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The region designator argument for the \emph{Get Dimension Handle Set} service shall be the designator of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{423.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a region template, a region specification, or a region realization.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{438.780}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{438.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The region designator argument for the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service shall be the designator of either a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{450.780}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region template or a region specification.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{474.640}{%
 \textbf{9.1.2 Relating region specifications and region realizations}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{498.779}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following relationships, established in the FDD, shall pertain to dimensions:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{510.779}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.962}{510.779}{400.038}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The available dimensions of a class attribute shall be the dimensions associated with that class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{522.778}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute in the FDD. The available dimensions of an instance attribute shall be the available%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{534.778}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimensions of the corresponding class attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{546.778}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.948}{546.778}{400.052}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The available dimensions of an interaction class shall be the dimensions associated with that class in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{558.778}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the FDD. The available dimensions of a sent interaction shall be the available dimensions of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{570.778}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interaction class specified in the \emph{Send Interaction With Regions} service invocation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{582.777}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.974}{582.777}{400.026}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 DDM services shall not be invoked for class attributes, instance attributes, interaction classes, or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{594.777}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 sent interactions that do not have available dimensions.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{606.777}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{606.777}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Each dimension in the FDD shall have either a default range specified in terms of the bounds [0, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{618.777}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimension’s upper bound) or shall have an \textbf{excluded indicator} specified in the Value When%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{630.777}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Unspecified Field of the FDD Dimension Table. Where a default range is specified for a dimension%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{642.776}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in the FDD and the dimension is not mentioned in a region specification, it is implicitly added, with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{654.776}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the specified default range, when creating a region realization. %
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{219}{218}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.3}{2}{Using regions}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.3.1}{2}{Region relationships}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{69.646}{%
 \textbf{9.1.3 Using regions}%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{93.646}{%
 \textbf{9.1.3.1 Region relationships}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following relationships, established through DDM services, shall pertain to regions:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{132.785}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{132.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The only way that a region specification can be created is by a federate successfully invoking the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{144.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 following services, in order:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{159.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.024}{159.784}{379.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Invoke the \emph{Create Region} service (see 9.2) to create a region with a specific set of dimensions.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{174.784}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.029}{174.784}{379.971}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For every dimension that was explicitly specified when that region was created, invoke the \emph{Set}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{186.784}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Range Bounds} service (see 10.32) to set the lower and upper bounds of the range of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{198.784}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 dimension for that region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{213.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 3)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.021}{213.783}{379.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Invoke \emph{Commit Region Modifications} (see 9.3) to inform the RTI about the changes to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{225.783}{379.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ranges of the dimensions specified in the preceding series of Set Range Bounds service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{237.783}{379.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocations.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{252.783}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region template is created when a federate invokes the \emph{Create Region} service. The region designa-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{264.783}{400.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 tor argument that is returned as a result of the \emph{Create Region} service is a designator of a region tem-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{276.782}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 plate only. It is not the designator of a region specification because the range bounds have not yet%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{288.782}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 been set for all of the dimensions of the region template followed by a successful invocation of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{300.782}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service for this region. Only after the Set\emph{ Range Bounds} service has%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{312.782}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 been successfully invoked for every dimension in the region, followed by a successful invocation of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{324.782}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service, is that region designator the designator of a region speci-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{336.781}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 fication. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.024}{348.781}{421.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.944}{348.781}{400.056}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a federate invokes the \emph{Register Object Instance With Region}, \emph{Associate Regions For Updates},%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{360.781}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Subscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions}, \emph{Subscribe Interaction Class With Regions}, \emph{Send}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{372.781}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Interaction With Regions}, or \emph{Request Attribute Value Update With Regions} service with that region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{384.781}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification designator as an argument, one or more region realizations are created. These region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{396.781}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 realizations, however, do not have designators.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.026}{408.780}{421.974}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{408.780}{400.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The specified dimensions of the region specification shall be the dimensions that are explicitly%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.987}{420.780}{400.013}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 provided when the \emph{Create Region} service is invoked to create that region specification. Invocation of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.987}{432.780}{400.013}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 neither the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service nor the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service for a particular%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.987}{444.780}{400.013}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region has any effect on what the specified dimensions of that region specification are.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.027}{456.780}{421.973}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.987}{456.780}{400.013}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The unspecified dimensions of a region realization shall be the available dimensions of the class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{468.779}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute, instance attribute, interaction class, or sent interaction with which the region realization is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{480.779}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 associated less the specified dimensions of the region specification from which the region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{492.779}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 realization is \textbf{derived}.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.026}{504.779}{421.974}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 e)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{504.779}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service can only either%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{519.779}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.031}{519.779}{379.969}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Create a region specification from a region template, or %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.986}{534.778}{400.014}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.034}{534.778}{379.966}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Modify the range bounds of an existing region specification and thereby also modify the range%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.026}{546.778}{379.974}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 bounds of all existing region realizations that are derived from that region specification.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.026}{561.778}{421.974}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 f)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.960}{561.778}{400.040}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a region realization is created by associating a region specification with an instance attribute,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{573.778}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a class attribute, an interaction class, or a sent interaction, additions may be made to the region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{585.778}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 realization by the RTI to account for default dimension values indicated in the FDD as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.985}{600.777}{400.015}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.030}{600.777}{379.970}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 All specified dimensions of the region specification shall be included in the region realization,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.025}{612.777}{379.975}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and the range associated with each specified dimension in the region realization shall be the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{624.786}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 range found in the region specification for the same dimension.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{639.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.033}{639.785}{379.967}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For each unspecified dimension of the region realization, if the FDD indicates a default range%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{651.785}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 other than the excluded indicator, this default range shall be added to the region realization.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{666.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 3)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.033}{666.785}{379.967}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 When a federate modifies a region specification from which region realizations have been%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{678.785}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 derived, the RTI shall fill in unspecified dimensions in the region realizations in this same%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{690.785}{379.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 manner.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{220}{219}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.3.2}{2}{Instance attribute relationships}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{69.786}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 g)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region specification may contain an empty set of ranges. The region realization derived from such%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{81.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a region specification shall contain only the dimensions for which the FDD defines a default range%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{93.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and that are available dimensions of the instance attribute, class attribute, interaction class, or sent%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{105.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interaction with which the region specification is being associated. This situation may result in a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{117.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region realization that contains no dimensions if all available dimensions have the excluded%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{129.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 indicator specified in the FDD; such a region realization shall not overlap with any other region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{141.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 realization, even the default region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If a federate invokes the \emph{Create Region} service but does not subsequently successfully invoke the \emph{Set Range}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{177.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Bounds} service for every dimension in the region, followed by a successful invocation of the \emph{Commit Region}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{189.784}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Modifications} service for the region, then the federate has not created a region specification. In particular,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{204.784}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 h)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{204.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If a federate invokes the \emph{Create Region} service and then does not invoke the \emph{Set Range Bounds}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{216.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service or invokes the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service for only some, but not all, of the dimensions that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{228.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 were specified when the region was created, followed by an invocation of the \emph{Commit Region}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{240.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Modifications} service for that region, the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service shall throw the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{252.783}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 “Invalid region” exception because each region designator that is passed to the \emph{Commit Region}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{264.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Modifications} service is required to have had the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service invoked at least once for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{276.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 all of its dimensions. The effects of the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service invocations that were made, if any,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{288.782}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 are still pending. They shall take effect if and when the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service has been invoked%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{300.782}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 at least once for all of the dimensions of the region, followed by the invocation of the \emph{Commit}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{312.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Region Modifications} service for that region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{324.782}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 i)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{324.782}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 If a federate invokes the \emph{Create Region} service, followed by at least one \emph{Set Range Bounds} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{336.782}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invocation for every one of the dimensions that were specified when the region was created, but%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{348.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 does not invoke the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service, the region continues to be only a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{360.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 template, not a region specification. The effects of the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service invocations are still%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{372.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 pending and shall take effect if and when the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service is successfully%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{384.781}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invoked for that region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{408.780}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The effects of invocation of the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service for a given region (template or specification) shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{420.780}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 remain pending until the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service is subsequently invoked for that region. If a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{432.780}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate invokes the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service repeatedly for a given dimension of a given region before%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.004}{444.780}{431.996}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 invoking the \emph{Commit Region Modifications} service for that region, the range values provided in the most%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.004}{456.780}{431.996}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 recent invocation of the \emph{Set Range Bounds} service shall become the range values for that dimension of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{468.779}{431.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region specification.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{492.640}{%
 \textbf{9.1.3.2 Instance attribute}\textbf{ }\textbf{relationships}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{516.779}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following relationships, established through DDM services, shall pertain to object classes, class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{528.778}{431.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attributes, object instances, and instance attributes:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{543.778}{421.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.968}{543.778}{400.032}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region realization other than the default region shall be used for update of an instance attribute if%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{555.778}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate owns the instance attribute and has used the instance attribute and region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{567.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 specification from which the region realization was derived as arguments either in the \emph{Register}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{579.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Object Instance With Regions} service or in the \emph{Associate Regions For Updates} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{594.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The default region shall be used for update of an instance attribute if and only if the corresponding%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{606.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class attribute has available dimensions and there is no other region realization used for update for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{618.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that instance attribute. This situation may occur if the \emph{Register Object Instance} service is used to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{630.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 register an instance of an object class that has attributes with available dimensions or if a region%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{642.784}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 association for update is removed via the \emph{Unassociate Regions for Updates} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{654.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Subsequently invoking the \emph{Unassociate Regions For Updates} service for the same (object instance,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{666.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region, attribute) triple shall cause that region not to be used for update of that instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{678.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Invoking the \emph{Associate Regions For Updates} service or the \emph{Unassociate Regions For Updates}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{690.784}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service with an empty set of regions shall make no changes to the set of associations of the instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{702.783}{400.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{221}{220}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.3.3}{2}{Interaction relationships}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Any region specifications used to generate region realizations associated with an instance attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{81.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 for update shall contain only dimensions that are a subset of the available dimensions of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{93.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute. The resulting region realizations shall have the same property.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{105.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate shall use a region for update of an instance attribute to assert properties of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{117.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute. These properties shall be used to limit reflection of the instance attributes when%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{129.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate invokes the \emph{Update Attribute Values} service. If a region other than the default%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{141.785}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region is used for update of a particular instance attribute by a joined federate and the joined federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{153.784}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 loses ownership of that instance attribute, that region shall no longer be used for update of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{165.784}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{180.784}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate may create and modify update region associations with an instance attribute that is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{192.784}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 owned by another joined federate or that is unowned. These associations shall not take effect until%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{204.784}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate making the associations has acquired ownership of the specified instance attri-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{216.783}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 bute. These associations shall take effect immediately upon acquiring ownership of the specified%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{228.783}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attributes.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{243.783}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 In all cases, if a joined federate divests ownership of an instance attribute with which an update%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{255.783}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region is associated, that association shall be lost, as if the \emph{Unassociate Regions For Updates} service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{267.783}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 had been invoked for that (object instance, region, attribute) triple. Update region associations that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{279.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 are lost shall not come into effect if the joined federate subsequently acquires ownership of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{291.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute unless the joined federate explicitly recreates the association.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{306.782}{421.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{306.782}{400.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region realization other than the default region shall be used for subscription of a class attribute if%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{318.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate has used the class attribute and a given object class and the region specification%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{330.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 from which the region realization was derived as arguments in the \emph{Subscribe Object Class Attributes}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{342.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{With Regions} service. Subsequently invoking the \emph{Unsubscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{354.781}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service for the same (object class, region, attribute) triple shall cause the region not to be used for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{366.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscription of that class attribute. Invoking the \emph{Subscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{378.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 service or the \emph{Unsubscribe Object Class Attributes With Regions }service with an empty set of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{390.781}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 regions shall make no changes to the set of subscriptions with region of the class attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{402.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Any region specifications used to generate region realizations associated with a class attribute for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{414.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 subscription shall contain only dimensions that are a subset of the available dimensions of that class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{426.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute. The resulting region realizations shall have the same property.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{438.780}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The default region shall be used for subscription of a class attribute if and only if that class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{450.780}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 has available dimensions, there is no other region realization used for subscription of that class attri-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{462.780}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 bute, and the joined federate is subscribed to that class attribute. Subsequently invoking the \emph{Unsub-}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{474.779}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{scribe Object Class Attributes} service for the same object class and attribute shall cause the default%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{486.779}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region not to be used for subscription of that class attribute. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{498.779}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate shall use a region for subscription of a class attribute to specify requirements for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{510.779}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 reflecting values of that class attribute’s analogous instance attributes.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{534.639}{%
 \textbf{9.1.3.3 Interaction relationships}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{558.778}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The following relationships, established through DDM services, shall pertain to interaction classes,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{570.778}{431.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 parameters, and interactions:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{585.778}{421.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.968}{585.778}{400.032}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region realization other than the default region shall be used for sending an interaction if the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{596.817}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate has used the interaction and a region specification from which the region realization%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{607.797}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 may be \textbf{derived} as arguments to an invocation of the \emph{Send Interaction With Regions }service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{618.777}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Any region associated with a sent interaction shall contain only dimensions that are a subset of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{630.777}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 available dimensions of the sent interaction. The default region shall be used for sending an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{642.777}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interaction of such a class during an invocation of the \emph{Send Interaction} service.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{654.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate shall use a region for sending an interaction to assert properties of that interaction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{666.785}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 when the \emph{Send Interaction With Regions} service is invoked.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{681.785}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{681.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A region realization other than the default region shall be used for subscription of an interaction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{693.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class if the joined federate has used the interaction class and the region specification from which the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{705.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region realization was derived as arguments in the \emph{Subscribe Interaction Class With Regions} service.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

\HLASourcePage{222}{221}
\HLAServiceBookmark{9.1.4}{2}{Calculating region overlaps}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Subsequently invoking the \emph{Unsubscribe Interaction Class With Regions} service for the same%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{81.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 (interaction class, region) pair shall cause the region not to be used for subscription of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{93.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interaction class. Invoking the \emph{Subscribe Interaction Class With Regions }service or the \emph{Unsubscribe}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{105.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Interaction Class With Regions} service with an empty set of regions shall make no changes to the set%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{117.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of subscriptions with region of the interaction class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{132.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Any region associated with an interaction class for subscription shall contain only dimensions that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{144.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 are a subset of the available dimensions of that interaction class. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{156.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The default region shall be used for subscription of that interaction class if and only if that interac-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{168.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 tion class has available dimensions, there is no other region realization used for subscription of that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{180.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 interaction class, and the joined federate is subscribed to that interaction class. Subsequently invok-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{192.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ing the \emph{Unsubscribe Interaction Class} service for the same interaction class shall cause the default%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{204.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 region not to be used for subscription of that interaction class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{216.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A joined federate shall use a region for subscription of an interaction class to establish requirements%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{228.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 for receiving interactions of that class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{252.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A set of region realizations used for update of instance attributes or for sending interactions shall be called%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{264.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 an \textbf{update region set}.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{288.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 A set of region realizations used for subscription of either class attributes or interaction classes shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{300.782}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 called a \textbf{subscription region set}.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{324.642}{%
 \textbf{9.1.4 Calculating region overlaps}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{348.781}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 An update region set and a subscription region set shall overlap if and only if a region exists in each set so%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{360.781}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that the two regions overlap. Two regions overlap if and only if all ranges of dimensions that are contained%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{372.781}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in both regions overlap pairwise. If two regions do not have any dimensions in common, they shall not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{384.781}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 overlap. Two ranges in the same dimension A = [a{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower}, a{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont upper}) and B = [b{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower}, b{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont upper}) shall overlap if and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{396.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 only if either a{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower} = b{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower }or (a{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower} < b{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont upper} and b{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont lower} < a{\fontsize{7.98pt}{9.48pt}\selectfont upper}) or the Allow Relaxed DDM switch is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{408.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 enabled and the RTI implementation makes the determination, based on implementation-specific criteria,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{420.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 that the ranges are sufficiently close to warrant an expanded interpretation of one or both ranges; neither%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{432.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 range may ever be reduced.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{456.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The normalization of federation data to [0, a particular dimension’s upper bound) for use with DDM%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{468.785}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 services shall be left to the federation. The effects of DDM services shall be independent of the time axis and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{480.784}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 HLA time management services.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{504.784}{432.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Figure 18 depicts a region with two dimensions.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

