 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{126.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 This clause describes miscellaneous services utilized by joined federates for performing such actions as the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{138.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 following:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{153.785}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{153.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Performing name-to-handle and handle-to-name transformations%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{168.785}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{168.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Getting and setting switch values%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{183.785}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{183.785}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Manipulating regions%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{198.784}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{198.784}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Getting update rate values.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{222.645}{%
 \textbf{10.1.1 Names}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{246.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 All class name arguments shall be completely specified, including all superclass names, with the exception%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{258.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 of the HLA root classes. The inclusion of HLAobjectRoot or HLAinteractionRoot shall be optional.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{282.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Each name in an FDD (object classes, interactions, attributes, parameters, dimensions, transportation types,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{294.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 order types) shall have a unique, and unpredictable, federation execution-wide handle.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{318.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 All names shall be case sensitive.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{342.643}{%
 \textbf{10.1.2 Switches}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{366.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The initial setting of RTI switches for a federation execution may be provided in the FDD(s) supplied to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{378.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 \emph{Create Federation Execution} service invocation. If no value is specified for a switch by the FDD(s) supplied%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{390.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 in the \emph{Create Federation Execution} service invocation, then the RTI will provide default values based on the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{402.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 switches defaults table in IEEE Std 1516.2-2025. Support services are provided that allow federates to get%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{414.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the value of any of the switches. Support services are also provided to set the local value of the per federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{426.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 switches that can be changed dynamically during federation execution.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{450.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The purpose of the switches is to allow a federate or federation to control certain characteristics of the RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{462.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 behavior when specific services are invoked. A basic description of each switch is given in IEEE Std%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{474.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 1516.2-2025. Additional descriptions of how the RTI behaves based on switch values are provided%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{486.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 throughout this document where appropriate. The following section, 10.1.2.1, provides information about%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{498.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the advisory switches (Object Class Relevance, Attribute Relevance, Interaction Relevance, and Attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{510.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Scope). The Auto-Provide Switch behavior is described in 6.1.9. The Convey Region Designator Sets%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{522.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Switch behavior is described in 9.1.7. The Service Reporting Switch, Send Service Reports to File Switch,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{534.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 and Exception Reporting Switch are described in 11.5. The Delay Subscription Evaluation Switch is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{546.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 described in 8.1.8. The Non-Regulated Grant Switch is described in 8.1.6. The Automatic Resign Directive%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{558.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Switch is described in 4.1.1 and 4.1.6. The Advisories Use Known Class Switch is described in 6.1.5 and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{570.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 6.23. The Allow Relaxed DDM Switch is described in 9.1.8 and E.9.1.8.%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{594.639}{%
 \textbf{10.1.2.1 Advisory switches}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{618.778}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The settings of the following per federate advisory switches may be modified by the switches support%
 }
