\HLASourcePage{245}{244}
\HLAServiceBookmark{10.1.3}{2}{Handle Normalization}
\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The enabling of an advisory switch directs that the RTI shall inform the joined federate, via the appropriate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 advisory notifications, whenever the conditions covered by that advisory change. The disabling of an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 advisory switch directs the RTI to cease informing the joined federate of changes in the conditions covered%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 by that advisory. When an advisory switch is disabled, all relevant notifications that would have been%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 delivered to the joined federate shall be lost, i.e., the RTI shall not save the relevant actions and send them to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate when a switch is subsequently enabled.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 There is, however, one case in which the RTI shall not inform a joined federate when specific conditions%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 covered by an advisory change, even if that advisory switch is enabled. Specifically, even if the Attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Scope Advisory Switch is enabled, there are some actions a joined federate could take that would cause an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{189.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 instance attribute to go out of scope with respect to that joined federate. Since these changes are a result of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{201.784}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate’s own action and the joined federate knows that the action will cause the instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{213.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 attribute to go out of scope, no out-of-scope advisory notification shall be given the joined federate. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{225.783}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 actions that could cause an instance attribute to go out of scope for the acting joined federate are as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{240.783}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{240.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate acquires ownership of the instance attribute.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{255.783}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{255.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate unsubscribes to the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute, and it is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{267.783}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 not subscribed to the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute with region.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{282.782}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{282.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The joined federate unsubscribes with region to the instance attribute’s corresponding class attribute%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{294.782}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 so that it is no longer subscribed to the class attribute (with or without region).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{318.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 These cases are referred to as implicit out-of-scope situations because no out-of-scope advisory notification%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{330.782}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 is generated.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{354.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Note that if a joined federate unsubscribes with or without region to an instance attribute’s corresponding%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{366.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 class attribute, but is still subscribed to that class attribute with some other region, it may or may not have%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{378.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 caused the instance attribute to go out of scope (assuming it was previously in scope). Since the joined%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{390.781}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 federate does not know if its removal has caused overlap to be lost with the update region set, in this case the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{402.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 joined federate relies on the RTI to inform it of whether the instance attribute has gone out of scope. Only if%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{414.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the joined federate completely removes all subscriptions (DM and DDM based subscriptions) can it know%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{426.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 with certainty that it is causing an implicit out-of-scope situation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{450.780}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 For purposes of determining whether the conditions covered by each advisory have changed, when the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{462.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 conditions required for sending each advisory become relevant at a given federate, the initial state of each%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{474.779}{432.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 advisory, as discerned by that federate, is as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{486.779}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.967}{486.779}{400.033}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Before a federate begins publishing an object class, the conditions covered by the Object Class%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{498.779}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Relevance Advisory Switch are assumed to be such that the registration of new object instances of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{510.779}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 the specified object class is not advised. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{522.779}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{522.779}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Before a federate begins publishing an interaction class, the interaction class is in the Interactions%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{534.778}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Turned Off state with respect to that federate (see Figure 13).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{546.778}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{546.778}{400.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Before a federate becomes the owner of an instance attribute, the instance attribute is in the Updates%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{558.778}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Turned Off state with regard to that federate (see Figure 15).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{570.778}{421.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.937}{570.778}{400.063}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Before a federate knows about an object instance, all of the instance attributes of that object instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{582.778}{400.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 are in the Attributes Out-of-Scope state with regard to the federate (see Figure 15).%
 }
 \HLAServiceComponentHeadingAt{606.638}{%
 \textbf{10.1.3 Handle Normalization}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{630.777}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 Some types of RTI handles have a normalized value that can be used to construct a point range for the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{642.777}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 appropriate dimension of that handle type [e.g., Federate Handle and HLAFederate dimension (see Table 9)].%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{654.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 The normalized handle value like the handle itself is originated by the RTI, federation execution-wide%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{666.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 unique, and unpredictable. The normalized handle values shall have no guarantee of continuity (i.e. they are%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{678.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 suitable only for a point range). The normalized handle values shall have no guarantee of uniqueness but%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{690.776}{432.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{12.00}{%
 given two equal handle instances, their normalized values shall also be equal.%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

