\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{69.786}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.978}{69.786}{482.022}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Interaction classes that are subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAadjust and HLAmanager.-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{81.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAfederation.HLAadjust%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{232.680}{81.785}{371.320}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 shall be acted on by the RTI. They permit a managing federate to adjust%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{93.785}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 how the RTI performs when responding to another federate and how it shall respond and report to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{105.785}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 the managing federate.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{117.785}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.941}{117.785}{482.059}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Interaction classes that are subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLArequest shall be acted on%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{129.785}{482.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 by the RTI. They shall cause the RTI to send subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{141.785}{482.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.022}{153.784}{503.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{153.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Interaction classes that are subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport shall be sent by the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{165.784}{482.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 RTI. They shall respond to interaction classes that are subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{177.784}{482.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLArequest class interactions. They shall describe some aspect of the federate, such as its object%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{189.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 class subscription tree.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{201.784}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.940}{201.784}{482.060}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Interaction classes that are subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAservice shall be acted on%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{213.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 by the RTI. They shall invoke HLA services on behalf of another federate. These interactions shall%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{225.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 cause the RTI to react as if the service was invoked by that other federate (for example, a managing%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{237.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 federate could change the time-regulating state of another federate).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{569.684}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{11.3.1 Extension of MOM interaction classes}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{593.823}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The MOM interaction classes may be extended by adding subclasses or parameters. There are three%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{605.823}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 categories of extension of MOM interaction classes as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{620.823}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{620.823}{482.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Classes of interaction that the RTI shall send (subclasses of HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport).%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{632.823}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall publish at the MOM leaf-class level (e.g., HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLA-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{644.822}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 report.HLAreportException). It shall send interactions containing all predefined parameters for that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{656.822}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction class. Valid methods for extending this type of MOM interaction class are as follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{671.822}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{671.822}{461.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Subclasses may be added to these MOM interaction classes. The RTI shall not send interactions%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{683.822}{461.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 of these subclasses. If joined federates subscribe to the subclass, they shall receive the full%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{695.821}{461.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction. If they subscribe to the class of which the extension is a subclass, the interaction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{707.821}{461.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 shall be promoted to the subscribed class, and any new parameters shall be lost.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{207.300}{526.666}{396.700}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Figure 20—MOM interaction class structure}%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

