 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{168.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 follows:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{183.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.025}{183.784}{461.975}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Subclasses may be added to any MOM interaction class. If a joined federate sends an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.019}{195.784}{461.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction of this class, the RTI shall receive a promoted version that shall contain only the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.018}{207.783}{461.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 parameters of the predefined interaction class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.977}{222.783}{482.023}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 2)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.022}{222.783}{461.978}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Parameters may be added to any MOM interaction class. If a joined federate sends an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.018}{234.783}{461.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction with extra parameters, the RTI shall receive the new parameters, but shall ignore%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.018}{246.783}{461.982}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 them and process only the predefined parameters.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.017}{261.783}{503.983}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.972}{261.783}{482.028}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Classes of interaction that shall be neither sent nor received by the RTI. These classes of interaction%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.976}{273.782}{482.024}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 shall be ignored by the RTI and may be formed in any way that is consistent with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.976}{285.782}{482.024}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 IEEE 1516.2 federation object model (FOM) development.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{315.383}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{10.98}{12.30}{%
 \textbf{11.4 MOM-related characteristics of the RTI}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{342.646}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{11.4.1 Normal RTI MOM administration}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{369.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI deals with MOM object classes and interaction classes in the following ways:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{381.785}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.983}{381.785}{482.017}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall publish all leaf object classes in Table 6 that are designated with a “P.”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{393.785}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.942}{393.785}{482.058}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 For each leaf object class in Table 6, the RTI shall publish all attributes in Table 8 for that object%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{405.785}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 class that are designated with a “P,” and no more.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{417.784}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.982}{417.784}{482.018}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall publish all leaf interaction classes in Table 7 that are designated with a “P.”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{429.784}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 d)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.943}{429.784}{482.057}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 In response to an interaction of class HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLArequest where the requested%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{441.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 information does not exist at the designated federate, the RTI shall send the corresponding%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{453.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction of class HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport with the appropriate values that indicate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{465.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 a NULL response. The conditions for a NULL response are given in Table 18. The appropriate value%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{477.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 and inclusion of a parameter in a NULL response is given in Table 20. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{492.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 1)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.024}{492.783}{461.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI may be required to provide an attribute or parameter whose value is undefined. For an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{504.783}{461.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 attribute or parameter having an array value, an undefined value shall be encoded as an empty%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{142.020}{516.783}{461.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 (zero-length) array.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{531.783}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 e)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{531.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 When sending an interaction of one of the leaf classes in Table 7 that is not a NULL response, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{543.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 RTI shall always supply all parameters listed in Table 9 for that interaction class, and no more.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{555.782}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 f)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.961}{555.782}{482.039}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall be actively subscribed to all leaf interaction classes in Table 7 that are designated with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{567.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 an “S.”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{579.782}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 g)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{579.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall be neither time-regulating nor time-constrained and shall never provide timestamps or%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{591.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 user-supplied tags with instance attribute updates, sent interactions, or deletion of object instances.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{603.781}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 h)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{603.781}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The RTI shall update the values of all attributes of instances of HLAmanager.HLAfederate found in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{615.781}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Table 8 using an update region set that contains a single region. The region used with each instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{627.781}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 attribute shall contain only the HLAfederate dimension as a specified dimension. The range for that%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{639.781}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 dimension shall be a point range around the normalized value (using the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{410.281}{639.781}{193.719}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Normalize Federate Handle}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{651.781}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 service) of the HLAfederateHandle attribute of that object instance%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{389.580}{652.515}{214.420}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.00}{10.08}{%
 .%
 }
\end{hlafixedpage}
\clearpage

