\thispagestyle{hla-body}
\begin{hlafixedpage}
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.383}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{10.98}{12.30}{%
 \textbf{11.5 Service reporting}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{94.806}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.HLAreportServiceInvocation interaction shall be generated by%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{106.806}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 the RTI whenever an HLA service is invoked, either by a particular joined federate or by the RTI at a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{118.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 particular joined federate, and the Service Reporting Switch is enabled for that particular joined federate.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{130.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The interaction shall be sent to subscribed federates if the Send Service Reports to File Switch is disabled for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{142.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 that joined federate; otherwise, the interaction shall be recorded in a service report log file. The initial setting%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{154.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 for these switches shall come from the FDD(s) supplied to the Create Federation Execution service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{166.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 invocation for the federation execution. If no value is specified for a switch, then the RTI will provide a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{178.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 default value based on the switches defaults table in IEEE Std 1516.2-2025. These switch settings shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{190.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 modifiable during a federation execution via the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{286.079}{190.804}{317.921}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Set Service Reporting Switch}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{402.240}{190.804}{201.760}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 and %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{421.980}{190.804}{182.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Set Send Service Reports}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{202.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{To File Switch}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{152.160}{202.804}{451.840}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 support services or the HLAmanager.HLAfederation.HLAadjust.HLAsetSwitches MOM%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{214.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interaction.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{238.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 If a joined federate is subscribed to the HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.HLAreportService-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{250.803}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Invocation interaction, all attempts to set the Service Reporting switch shall fail. If a joined federate has the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{262.803}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Service Reporting switch enabled, that joined federate shall not be able to subscribe to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{274.803}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.-HLAreportServiceInvocation interaction class.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{298.803}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Similar to service reporting, the Exception Reporting Switch controls whether the RTI will generate a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{310.802}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.HLAexception interaction whenever a federate-invoked HLA%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{322.802}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 service generates an exception. Unlike service reporting, a federate may be both subscribed to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{334.802}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.HLAexception interaction and have the Exception Reporting Switch%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{346.802}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 enabled.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{370.662}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{11.5.1 Argument encoding}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{394.801}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The HLAmanager.HLAfederate.HLAreport.HLAreportServiceInvocation interaction uses the HLA-%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{406.801}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 argument fixed record data type for its HLAsuppliedArguments and HLAreturnedArgument parameters to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{418.801}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 encode service call parameters and return values respectively. HLAsuppliedArguments is an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{430.801}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAargumentList where the number of the elements in the list shall match the number of arguments in the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{442.800}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 corresponding service narrative. If an argument is specified as optional and the argument was not used, it%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{454.800}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 will be included in the list as Null. If the service does not take any arguments the list shall be empty. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{466.800}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 textual depiction encoded in the HLAargumentName field for the HLAsuppliedArguments elements and the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{478.800}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAreturnedArgument is RTI implementation dependent and intended for descriptive purposes only. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{490.800}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAreturnedArgument parameter shall contain all of the return arguments of the corresponding service%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{502.799}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 narrative. If the service does not return a value or the HLAsuccessIndicator is HLAfalse, the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{514.799}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 HLAargumentType field of the HLAreturnedArgument shall be Null.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{538.799}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The encoding of argument values for the HLAargumentValue field shall follow a simple format similar to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{550.799}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 JSON [B2]. The following basic elements are defined with all characters encoded using Unicode:%
 }
