 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{69.786}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{69.786}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 To provide as natural a mapping to the abstract interface specification as possible.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{81.785}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{81.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 To help prevent as many common federate programming errors as practical. This goal includes%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{93.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 compile-time type safety as well as dynamic memory management errors.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{105.785}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{105.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 To provide flexibility to RTI implementers while adhering to a common API (as used by the federate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{117.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 programmer) and without adding significant overhead.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{129.785}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{129.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 To support dynamic link compatibility that allows federates to switch between RTI implementations%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{141.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 without recompiling.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.645}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{12.12.1 Dynamic link compatibility}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{189.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Dynamic link compatibility shall allow a federate to switch from one RTI C++ implementation to another%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{201.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 without recompiling or relinking. To support dynamic link compatibility between implementations, RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{213.783}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 C++ implementations and federates shall meet the following three requirements:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{237.783}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 a)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.966}{237.783}{482.034}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 All RTI implementations and federates shall be built against a standard set of header files (see%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{249.783}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Annex C). Header files shall be provided in a directory named RTI.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{261.783}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 b)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{261.783}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The symbols defined in the header files shall be found in identically named dynamic link libraries%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{273.783}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 provided by RTI implementations and dynamically linked with federates.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{285.782}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 c)%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.984}{285.782}{482.016}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 RTI implementations and federates shall be built on compatible platforms. The term “platform”%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{297.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 includes operating system version, compiler version, Application Binary Interface (ABI), and choice%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{309.782}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 of compiler and linker flags.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{333.642}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{12.12.1.1 RTI Libraries}%
 }
