 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{369.781}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Many programming errors in C++ can be traced back to the improper use of the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{445.980}{370.369}{158.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{delete}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{481.920}{369.781}{122.080}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 operator.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{381.781}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Frequently, this tendency is a result of poor programming practice, rather than an inherent limitation of the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{393.781}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 C++ programming language. Considerable effort has been made to help prevent memory corruption and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{405.780}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 leaks resulting from the misuse of the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{242.940}{406.368}{361.060}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{delete}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{278.940}{405.780}{325.060}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 operator in the C++ API.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{429.780}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 In particular, the federate programmer never explicitly deletes objects exchanged with the RTI. Simple%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{441.780}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 objects are passed by value. More complex objects are either passed by constant reference%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{453.780}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 (i.e., %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{110.820}{454.367}{493.180}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{T const \&}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{166.021}{453.780}{437.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ) or passed as a %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{230.880}{454.367}{373.120}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{unique\_ptr<T>}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{308.820}{453.780}{295.180}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 object. In all three cases, the C++ compiler prevents%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{465.779}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 the federate programmer from calling the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{257.640}{466.367}{346.360}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{delete}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{293.640}{465.779}{310.360}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 operator on the object.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{489.779}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 As explained in 12.12.6, the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{212.700}{490.367}{391.300}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{unique\_ptr<T>}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{293.940}{489.786}{310.060}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 implements the strong memory ownership and transfer%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{501.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 semantics of the %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{157.440}{502.373}{446.560}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{std::unique\_ptr<T>}%
 }
