 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.786}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The variable, variant, and fixed array encoders shall have both non-templated and templated classes. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{81.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 templated versions shall be called HLAvariableArrayT, HLAvariantRecordT, and HLAfixedArrayT%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{93.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 respectively. They shall contain a single template parameter that defines the type of data encoded in the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{105.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 arrays, or in the variant case the type of data encoded in the discriminant. Functions that refer to the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{117.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 DataElement type in the non-template versions shall instead refer to the defined template parameter in the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{129.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 template versions.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{153.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The encoded data generated by handle encoding helpers shall use the corresponding HLA<type>Handle data%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{165.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 type as defined in HLAstandardMIM. Handle decoders shall not attempt to check the (semantic) validity of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{177.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
