 . In fact, all exceptions in the C++ API inherit from a class named %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{445.079}{682.369}{158.921}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Exception}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{499.020}{681.781}{104.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 . This%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{693.781}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 hierarchy allows all exceptions in the C++ API to be caught as a single base class. The %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{445.680}{694.369}{158.320}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Exception}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{499.620}{693.781}{104.380}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 class%
