 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{165.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 A CallbackResponse message indicating if an exception occurred and using the generic%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{177.784}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ExceptionData message. This message is sent from the federate to the RTI.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{201.784}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The Session layer provides a sequence number in the message header that enables:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{225.783}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{225.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 A federate to match call requests with call responses;%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.021}{237.783}{503.979}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.981}{237.783}{482.019}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 An RTI to match callback requests with callback responses.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{261.783}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The sequence number is also used for other purposes, e.g. error checking and session resumption. It is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{273.783}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 specified in section 12.13.5.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{297.643}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{12.13.3.2 Services }%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{321.782}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 All the HLA services in Clause 4 through Clause 10 are implemented in the Federate Protocol with the%
