 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.020}{105.785}{503.980}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{105.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Sequence number: }%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{210.959}{105.785}{393.041}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Each message shall have a sequence number provided by the sending%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{117.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 component (separate for federate and RTI). The sequence number shall be represented as a 32 bit%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{129.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 unsigned integer with the most significant bit reserved to indicate an invalid sequence number (i.e.,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{141.785}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 values >= 2\textasciicircum{}31 are invalid). Sequence numbers shall be strictly increasing within the range 0 to%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.980}{153.784}{482.020}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 2\textasciicircum{}31-1. Upon reaching the value 2\textasciicircum{}31-1 (0x7fffffff), the next sequence number shall be reset to 0. In%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{165.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 practice, these sequence number values will be unique as the size of message history buffers shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{177.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 limited, see section 12.13.4.4.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{189.784}{503.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{189.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Session ID:}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{170.578}{189.784}{433.422}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Session ID that uniquely identifies a session for a given RTI. The Session ID shall be%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{201.784}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 assigned by the RTI. The same Session ID shall be used for all messages for a given session. The%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{213.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 value zero (0) shall indicate that no session exists.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{225.783}{503.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{225.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Last received message number:}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{256.619}{225.783}{347.381}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The sequence number for the last successfully received messages%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{237.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 as specified by the other component. This value can be used for managing the message history%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{249.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 buffers. Only sequence numbers for HLA service messages shall be considered when determining%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{261.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 the last received message excluding any control messages (e.g., Resume Request and Resume%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{273.783}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Response). When no last received message exists, an invalid sequence number shall be used. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.019}{285.782}{503.981}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{121.979}{285.782}{482.021}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{Message type}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{178.919}{285.782}{425.081}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 : Indicates the type of message.%
 }
