 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{69.120}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{12.00}{13.44}{%
 \textbf{E.8 Time management}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{101.363}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{10.98}{12.30}{%
 \textbf{E.8.1 Overview}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{126.786}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 At the federation level, this specification provides a variety of time management services to control the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{138.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 advancement of all joined federates along the time axis. These services allow multiple joined federates with%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{150.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 differing internal federation time advancement strategies to interoperate in a meaningful way. While the%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{162.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 strategy chosen for advancing federation time is an extremely important consideration in the design of a%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{174.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 simulation, the format of how federation time is represented is of equal importance.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{198.785}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 It is very important for all federation members to agree upon a common set of key federation time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{210.784}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 characteristics that apply across the full federation. In addition to defining certain characteristics of the time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{222.784}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 axis, it is also important to define the lookahead characteristics of both federates and federations. It is%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{234.784}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 important to recognize that there are semantic differences between the way federation time is represented for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{246.784}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 the purpose of advancing federation time versus calculating lookahead. When advancing federation time,%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{258.784}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 federation time can be considered to be an absolute value on a federation timeline, and thus federation time%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{270.783}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 comparisons can be drawn to determine if one federation time value is greater than another. Lookahead, in%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{282.783}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 contrast, represents a duration of federation time, which can be added to absolute federation time values but%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{294.783}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 is not generally used for comparison purposes. For this reason, federation time is defined using two abstract%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{306.783}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 data types (ADTs), %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{168.120}{307.371}{435.880}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTime}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{234.060}{306.783}{369.940}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 and %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{253.500}{307.371}{350.500}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTimeInterval}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{367.441}{306.783}{236.559}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 .%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{330.782}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Each of the specific language APIs contain ADTs for %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{317.102}{331.370}{286.898}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTime}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{383.042}{330.782}{220.958}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 and %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{405.542}{331.370}{198.458}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTimeInterval}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{519.482}{330.782}{84.518}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 .%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{342.782}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 These ADTs each define a set of interfaces for which implementations shall be provided before a federation%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{354.782}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 execution that utilizes time management services can take place. It is the responsibility of the federate/%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{366.782}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 federation %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{144.993}{366.782}{459.007}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 developer(s) %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{209.488}{366.782}{394.512}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 to %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{231.809}{366.782}{372.191}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 furnish %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{274.681}{366.782}{329.319}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 concrete %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{323.015}{366.782}{280.985}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 implementations %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{404.256}{366.782}{199.744}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 of %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{427.082}{367.370}{176.918}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTime}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{507.603}{366.782}{96.397}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{379.369}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{LogicalTimeInterval}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{203.943}{378.782}{400.057}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 interfaces.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{402.781}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Additionally, each of the language APIs also provide default concrete implementations of these two ADTs%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{414.781}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 based on the float 64 data type. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{438.641}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{E.8.1.1 Messages}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.002}{462.780}{513.998}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 While this specification states no explicit requirements on the order of delivery of RO messages, an RTI%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{474.780}{513.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 implementation may provide a more predictable order of delivery. A number of factors are considered by an%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.003}{486.780}{513.997}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 RTI when determining the order in which RO messages are received, including the following:%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{100.024}{510.780}{503.976}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ---%
