 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{321.642}{514.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \textbf{E.9.1.8 Allow Relaxed DDM}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.998}{345.781}{514.002}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The Allow Relaxed DDM switch was introduced to accommodate RTI implementations of DDM that do not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{357.781}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 fully comply with strict region overlap requirements in previous Interface Specifications. The purpose of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{369.781}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 Relaxed DDM is to trade off reduced filtering with improvements in the efficiency of managing and%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{381.781}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 calculating region overlaps. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{405.780}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 An RTI implementation may choose to implement DDM such that the behavior of DDM filtering does not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{417.780}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 change when the Allow Relaxed DDM switch is enabled. This result is the same as an RTI choosing%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{89.999}{429.780}{514.001}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 implementation-specific criteria for region overlaps that is always false.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{459.383}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{10.98}{12.30}{%
