 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{433.140}{484.806}{170.860}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 ), this service does not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{496.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 allow an object instance to be used as an argument; only an object class can be used. If an update for%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{508.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 attributes of a specific object instance is needed, the object management service should be used. As a request%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{520.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 that takes an object instance is already quite specific, additional DDM filtering based on regions is not%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{532.805}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 needed for such cases. %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{556.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 A single %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{126.660}{556.804}{477.340}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Request Attribute Value Update With Regions}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{311.040}{556.804}{292.960}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 service invocation for an object class may generate%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{568.804}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 many %
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{114.780}{568.804}{489.220}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Provide}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{148.621}{568.804}{455.379}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 \emph{Attribute Value Update †}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{251.341}{568.804}{352.659}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 service invocations at instance attribute-owning joined federates (at%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{580.804}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 least one for each object instance of the class for which the joined federate owns a requested attribute). This%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{592.804}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 situation will generate a nonpredictable “storm” of “interrupts” and possibly cause the timing behavior of%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.001}{604.804}{513.999}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 real-time federates to become unpredictable. This might be an unwise thing to do in a real-time federation.%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{640.140}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{12.00}{13.44}{%
 \textbf{E.11 Management object model (MOM)}%
 }
 \HLAFixedBlock{90.000}{666.786}{514.000}{\rmfamily\raggedright}{9.96}{11.16}{%
 The defined MOM functionality is necessary for successful federation execution operation and can be%
